[5071]={"'Ahhhh. Esa comida me ha sentado de maravilla, . Si no hubieras estado ahí para ayudarme a conseguir lo que necesitaba, no creo que me sintiera ni la mitad de satisfecho de lo que estoy ahora. ¿Alguna vez te han dicho que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]} bastante decente?'","Lleva al alcalde algo que lo alivie (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con el alcalde Pieblanco","En la zona de la Feria de los Granjeros hay objetos que podrían aliviar las molestias del alcalde.\
\
Deberías recoger un objeto que ayude a calmar lo que necesita el alcalde.","El alcalde Pieblanco se encuentra en la Feria de los Granjeros, en Delagua.\
\
Debes hablar con el alcalde Pieblanco.","Has aliviado al alcalde (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se dice que Will Pieblanco, alcalde de Cavada Grande, es el hobbit más gordo de la Cuaderna del Oeste (y quizá de más allá).\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento al que está asociada. </rgb>","'¡Qué festín! La Feria de los Granjeros es mi festival favorito del año, ${PLAYER}. Insisto en probar todos los platos que se ofrecen en el mercado.\
\
'El problema es que, a veces, pruebo algo bastante alarmante y necesito alivio. ¿Me ayudarás?'","No le has llevado al alcalde lo que te pidió (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","No le lleves al alcalde el objeto equivocado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Alcalde Gordo"},
[5081]={"Odovacar Bolger te ha prestado los servicios de su sabuesa, Verónica, para rastrear al misterioso \\qJinete Negro\\q. Te dijo que siguieras a Verónica dondequiera que fuera, y ella encontraría al intruso.","'¡Fogo debería avergonzarse por asustar a los cerdos del Sr. Bolger!'","'¡Ese tonto sobrino mío debería saber que no se asusta a la gente así!'","'¡Gracias a ti, ${PLAYERNAME:Frontero[m]|Frontera[f]}, por encontrar a ese tonto Albo!'","Odovacar Bolger está seguro de que el misterio del intruso de negro pronto se resolverá.","'¿De qué capa hablas? No veo ninguna capa.'","El destino del Jinete Negro","'¿Uno de los Albo está detrás del susto? ¿Cuál de ellos?'","'¿Llamaste a los Oficiales por mi sobrino, Fogo? ¿No? Qué pena....'","'No hubo daño en la broma, ¿verdad?'","'¡No más tonterías de ese \\qJinete Negro\\q, gracias a ti!'","Verónica olfatea la capa, huele el aire por un momento y luego ladra emocionada.","'¿Qué? ¿Qué Jinete Negro? ¿Yo? ¡De todas las cosas absurdas...! Oh, esta capa negra... sí, la he visto antes. ¡La cosí yo!\
\
'Esa capa la cosí para mi sobrino holgazán, Fogo. Y apenas me dio las gracias. Si quieres hablar con él, seguro que está en la Perca Dorada en Cepeda, pidiendo bebidas.\
\
'Me preguntaba para qué era esa capa. Se comportaba muy misterioso con ella. La tomaré de vuelta, muchas gracias, y ve a hablar con Fogo.''","Muestra la capa negra a Greta Albo","Odovacar Bolger está en su casa en el centro de Bolgovado, al norte de sus pocilgas.\
\
Deberías regresar con Odovacar Bolger y contarle lo que has aprendido sobre el \\qJinete Negro\\q.","Greta Albo está en Bolgovado.\
\
Verónica te ha llevado hasta Greta Albo. ¿Podría ser ella el misterioso \\qJinete Negro\\q?","'Supongo que no sería correcto denunciar a ese tonto a los Oficiales. Pero me pregunto quién será ese \\qSeñor\\q, y por qué querría gastarme esta broma tan terrible. ¿No pensarás... que Lotho... ¡no!\
\
'Bueno, no hay manera de probar nada, pero si Lotho quiere comprar mi granja, tendrá que esperar mucho tiempo, ¡te lo aseguro! ¡Se necesitará mucho más que esta pequeña \\qbroma\\q para que yo deje mi tierra!\
\
'Muchas gracias por todo tu trabajo. Puede que me hayas salvado de hacer una tontería. Por favor, acepta esta pequeña recompensa por tu ayuda.'","'No vas a contarle a los Oficiales sobre esa pequeña broma, ¿verdad?'","Verónica corre de vuelta con Odovacar","'¡Quiero que averigües quién ha estado rondando mis pocilgas!'","'Si hubiera sabido lo que tramaba Fogo, nunca le habría cosido esa capa.'","'Ve y dile al viejo Odovacar que no tenía malas intenciones -- ¡solo pensé que sería una broma graciosa! Odo probablemente está en su casa en el centro de Bolgovado, al norte de sus pocilgas.''","'¿Ya sabes quién ha estado rondando mis pocilgas?'","'Ah, bueno, supongo que has descubierto mi pequeño secreto. ¡Pensamos que sería muy divertido!\
\
'Verás, conocí a un tipo hace unos días, mientras bebía, se hacía llamar \\qEl Señor\\q. Dijo que era un viejo amigo de Odo y que quería gastarle una broma. Me dijo que consiguiera una capa negra y me dio algo de dinero para rondar la granja de Odovacar por la noche.\
\
'¡Bueno! ¡Seguro que no crees que quería hacer daño! ¡Jamás! ¿Ese Señor? No lo he visto desde entonces, ahora que lo pienso. Al menos saqué algo de dinero para cerveza. Oh, sí... Prometo no hacerlo de nuevo. ¡Esos lobos casi me atrapan! ¡No volveré a correr por la noche, eso seguro!'","Fogo Albo se encuentra en la Perca Dorada en Cepeda, al sureste de Bolgovado.\
\
La sabuesa de Odovacar Bolger, Verónica, te llevó hasta Greta Albo, quien te dijo que hizo la capa para su sobrino, Fogo. Fogo Albo es muy probablemente el \\qJinete Negro\\q. Deberías buscarlo.","'¡No temas! Mi sabuesa, Verónica, rastreará a ese \\qJinete Negro\\q con solo olfatear su capa. ¡Es la mejor cazadora de las Cuatro Cuadernas! Maggot puede presumir de su Grip, Fang y Wolf todo lo que quiera, pero yo apuesto por Verónica contra todos ellos.\
\
'Solo sigue a Verónica donde te guíe y verás. ¡Ella encontrará al intruso!''","No más \\qcabalgatas\\q nocturnas para mí... ¡demasiados lobos por ahí!","'¡Ahora no venderé mi granja por ningún precio!'","Sigue a Verónica hasta el \\qJinete Negro\\q","'Ve y habla con mi sobrino holgazán, Fogo, y pregúntale en qué ha estado. Seguro que lo encuentras pidiendo bebidas en la Perca Dorada, camino a Cepeda.'"},
[5083]={"'While travelling through the marsh, you have seen for yourself the rot that has consumed the forests of Adagím, or as it is better known in this time, the Moulderwood. This rot is known as the Pale Blight. You may have seen how it affected some of the lands to the west as well.\
\
'The Kintai here are doing everything we can to fight back against this infection, but our efforts seem to be a losing battle. This used to be a beautiful and green land until years ago when the Ordâkhai invaded and cracked the earth with the Din of Stone. That unleashed a pestilence that killed the trees, poisoned our waters, and caused fungal growths to appear everywhere.'\
\
Tálbiral looks distraught from recalling the events.\
\
'Sorry, friend. I need but a moment.'","'If you choose to help, I have many tasks that could use an extra hand.\
\
'I know not of the others as I remain within Laivárth, but I am certain they will be in need of help as well.\
\
'Thank you for giving me the chance to tell you of these lands. Be safe, adventurer. Adagím is no longer a forgiving place.'","Learn about Adagím from Tálbiral","'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I am Tálbiral and this grove is Laivárth. Welcome.\
\
'You do not seem familiar with Adagím. This marsh can be quite dangerous. Please, allow me to tell you more.'","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 1","Tálbiral clears his throat and readies himself to speak again.\
\
'Thank you. These events have caused us so much pain. They can be difficult to recall.\
\
'We are doing what we can, but my people have abandoned many of our groves already and left them to fester with rot and become overwhelmed with the beasts of the forest, now twisted by the blight consuming them.\
\
'This grove, Laivárth, and the main settlement to the east, Sul Madásh, are the last that remain unspoiled. Though as you can see, it is not without a cost.\
\
'I worry this land and my people will eventually fall. You are either brave or naive to come here, ${CLASS}. Though if you wish to help, there is much you can do in these marshes.'","Speak with Tálbiral to learn about the the Pale Blight's impact on Adagím and how the Kintai are trying to fight it.","Speak with Tálbiral"},
[5084]={"Dáthlil has received a scout's report that they have had strange sightings to the south and they believe they have located the source of the Pale Blight.","'You return. I trust that means you were victorious in defeating the beast of which our scout spoke?'\
\
You tell Dáthlil what happened at the entrance to the ruins of Nagakhêdi's wonder.\
\
'So you have! We have hope for the first time in many years thanks to you!\
\
'Could this really be the end of this blight raging in our lands? That foul monster must have been the reason the blight has been raging in recent months, and you put a stop to it. We will continue searching the area near the wonder, but what else could have been causing this pestilence?\
\
'Thank you again my friend. We are eternally grateful.'","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 10","'I am glad to see you. Our scouts have found the source of the blight.\
\
'We believe it to be in the ruins of an ancient wonder that was abandoned many years ago known to us as the Folly of Nagakhêdi.\
\
'When you are ready, head south and see if you can confirm what our scouts have found, and put and end to this plague.'","Speak with Dáthlil","Speak with Dáthlil to learn more about the scout's report","You have defeated the morroval that attacked you near the ruins of Nagakhêdi and is believe to be the source of the Pale Blight. Speak with Dáthlil about your success.","'Are you ready to travel south and stop this evil?\
\
'If our scout's report is true, they have spotted a beast unseen in these lands before. This must be the source of the blight!\
\
'Put an end to it.'"},
[5085]={"Tálbiral has asked for your help with checking trees within Laivárth for signs of rot so that they can be cleansed.","'It is as I feared. I am failing to keep Laivárth safe. This grove used to be unspoiled as well, but the signs are clear. It has begun to succumb to the rot. I will continue to defend the grove until my dying breath.\
\
'Those chieftains in Sul Madásh have abandoned us here, and many withdrew to the settlement. They will provide no aid to us, nor would I ask of it from them.\
\
'So it falls to the kindness of strangers. If you do wish to be of help, I have tasks that could use an adventurer like yourself.'","'Laivárth has not been safe from the Pale Blight. Though I am doing what I can to keep it safe.\
\
'I could use your help inspecting the trees of the grove for signs of rot. It must be cleansed early to prevent it spreading further.'","Blighted trees in Laivárth inspected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You found trees that have been infected by the Pale Blight within Laivárth. Return to Tálbiral so he knows to cleanse them from the grove.","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 2","Speak with Tálbiral","Inspect blighted trees in Laivárth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5086]={"Return to Tálbiral","'Welcome back. Were you able to find signs of the blight outside of the grove?'\
\
You tell Tálbiral of what you observed in the lands outside of Laivárth and how there is rot closing in everywhere.\
\
'That confirms what I have seen myself. We are running out of time to save Laivárth.\
\
'You have my thanks for looking into this for me and confirming my fears. I believe this will be of help identifying what we need to focus on cleansing from our forests.'","Inspect samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reach blight area","'I fear now that the blight is consuming Laivárth. I must put a stop to it.\
\
'${CLASS}, would you go out and further inspect the blight in the area outside of the grove and return with your findings? That may give us some indication of what is causing the blight to spread the fastest so that we can fight back this infection.'","Tálbiral has asked that you check the area surrounding Laivárth and gather samples of the blight for him to inspect.","Tálbiral has asked that you check the area surrounding Laivárth and inspect blighted areas to learn more about it.","You have inspected the blight surrounding Laivárth. Return to Tálbiral with the information you gathered.","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 3","Samples inspected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5087]={"You found Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother. Speak with her about the Pale Blight and how Laivárth is being consumed by it.","'Greetings, ${CLASS}. What brings you here to the Hill of the Mother?'\
\
You tell Irsinith about how Laivárth is losing the battle against the Pale Blight and that Tálbiral sent you to her to ask for her help.\
\
'As the warden of Amûma, my place is here. I must do everything I can to stop the rot inside, but as this affliction is killing the mother tree, I feel powerless.\
\
'Thank you for bringing me this word from the grove. I ask for a moment please to think on what I must do.'","Find Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother","Speak to Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother","Tálbiral has asked you to find and speak with Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother. She will want to know about how the Pale Blight is consuming Laivárth.","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 4","You see someone mourning near the tree","'I do not know what more I can do to prevent Laivárth from succumbing to the Pale Blight.\
\
'The chieftains of Sul Madásh...'\
\
Tálbiral looks filled with anger at the thought of the chieftains.\
\
'They have abandoned this grove and will do nothing to help. I am at a loss, my friend.\
\
'If you are willing, I ask that you travel to the Hill of the Mother to the east and seek out the warden there. Her name is Irsinith. She should know that the blight is winning the flight in Laivárth, and she may have spoken with Amûma and have more knowledge of how to stop the bleeding.'"},
[5088]={"'Have you had a chance to see the sap that weeps from Amûma?'\
\
You give Irsinith the sap you have gathered.\
\
'As you can see here in this sap, it appears bloody and diseased. You can see the rot festering inside even a small amount.\
\
'I feel now that Amûma herself is speeding up the death of Adagím. The affliction in her roots stretches deep into the earth and is killing the ground beneath our feet. She does not speak to me as she once did and the rare words I do hear are poisoned.\
\
'This pains me deeply and it is because of this, that I do not know how I can help Laivárth. Our mother tree may even be the cause of the grove dying.'","You have gathered sap from Amûma. Return to Irsinith with it so that she can show you the signs of the Pale Blight.","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 5","Sap gathered from Amûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather sap from Amûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Irsinith has asked you to gather sap from the trunk of the mother tree and return it to her so that she can show you how the Pale Blight is rotting within.","'I am saddened to hear about the grove. I will do what I can to help Tálbiral.\
\
'I understand how he must feel and I know all too well that the chieftains of Sul Madásh are not able to give much aid to those of us outside of the settlement.\
\
'I fear Amûma is not fairing any better than Laivárth as she is succumbing to the Pale Blight more with each passing day. As the warden here, I ask that you go and see for yourself to understand how nothing is safe from this pestilence. Gather the sap that you can find seeping from the mother tree herself and bring it to me. I will show you how the rot can be found within.'","Bring the sap from the mother tree to Irsinith"},
[5089]={"'Welcome, outsider. What brings you to Sul Madásh and caused you to brave the harsh lands of Adagím?'\
\
You tell Dáthlil of how Laivárth and Amûma are falling to the blight and that Irsinith sent you with the news and a request for help if they have learned more of the Pale Blight. Dáthlil looks relieved to hear any news about her daughter.\
\
'I am glad that you have seen Irsinith and that she is holding on as best she can. This blight consuming Laivárth and even the mother tree is most dire. I am sad to tell you that Sul Madásh is losing this battle against the pestilence that ravages our land. We are doing what we can, but many are losing hope.\
\
'If you wish to help us here, please speak with my husband Ildimár. He will know more of what needs to be done around the settlement. I will send word to Irsinith as I miss her dearly.'","Speak with Dáthlil","You found the chieftains of Sul Madásh. Speak with Dáthlil and bring her the news of the Pale Blight from her daughter, Irsinith.","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 6","You found the chieftains of Sul Madásh. Dáthlil has asked you to speak with her husband Ildimár and learn more about the settlement.","You see the chieftains of Sul Madásh engaged in a discussion","Speak with Ildimár","'Greetings. As Dáthlil said, I too am glad to hear word from our daughter. I am sad to hear about her circumstances, and I wish that she would come to the settlement, though I understand her duty is to Amûma. She makes us proud with her devotion.\
\
'She spoke the truth that Sul Madásh is suffering these days. The infection can be found in the trees within our walls despite our best efforts to cleanse the signs we see.\
\
'We are trying to identify the Pale Blight and put an end to this, so all help is accepted.'","'Bring word of Amûma to the chieftains of Sul Madásh.\
\
'Tálbiral feels they have failed our people and I have my struggles with them as well...'\
\
Irsinith pauses for a moment in thought, staring up at the Mother Tree.\
\
'They are my mother and father, and they have begged me to return home time and again, but my place is here, as her warden.\
\
'I may not be able to do much to prevent the rot from spreading, but they may know more in the settlement as the scholars retreated there as our groves fell. They also may be in need of help from a ${CLASS} like yourself.'","Find the chieftains in Sul Madásh","Irsinith has asked you to travel to Sul Madásh and speak with the chieftains there. They will want to know of the Pale Blight's effect on Amûma and Laivárth."},
[5090]={"'As you can see, the entire land is consumed outside of this sanctuary, and even some land within its borders.\
\
'It is disheartening to be fighting against this threat as it turns our very earth against us. We have thus far kept the threat at bay all these years, but we know we are losing the battle and Sul Madásh will soon be lost if the spread is not stopped.\
\
'Though after all these years we recently had Rangers from the north arrive and they speak about how they have seen similar things in their lands. They bring knowledge that may be able to help our people. Please, speak with them as they have spoken of how they could use someone like yourself.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the lands of Adagím","Ildimár has asked that you look out over the lands of Adagím from where they stand so you can see how bad the Pale Blight has ravaged the land.","The lands outside of Sul Madásh appear endless and covered in fungal rot","'${PLAYER}! I did not think we would encounter you in these southern lands, so far from Imlad Morgul, but it seems Viznak was right after all! I believed his confidence sprang from a misunderstanding of the geography and the sheer size of Harad... but perhaps it was instead his knowledge of your penchant for adventure, and your desire to aid any who have need.\
\
'You know of the evils Lhaereth the Stained worked in Imlad Morgul and in Agarnaith. Word came to us that a pestilence not dissimilar to that of the Lady of Blight had taken root in these lands, long ago, and we thought to investigate. We wish now to help where we can.\
\
'There may be something we can do to help these people... especially now that we are together again! Please return to me when you can as we will need your help with the task.'","Ildimár has told you that Rangers from the north arrived in Sul Madásh to fight back the Pale Blight and could likely use your help.","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 7","You have seen just how far the Pale Blight has spread through Adagím and how so little of it remains unspoiled. You should speak with Ildimár now that you know more of what they are up against.","Speak with Ildimár","Speak with Faeron","'There is much you can do to help here in Sul Madásh. There are many here who could use your help if you ask around the settlement, and I am certain they will be grateful for the assistance.\
\
'We are usually wary of outsiders, especially in times like this, but you helped our daughter, Irsinith, so you are most welcome. As I mentioned, this settlement is slowly but surely succumbing to this blight. And with the infection, you will face many dangers here in Adagím as the creatures here have become twisted and vile with rot. The threats grow by the day.\
\
'I am certain you have seen how the blight has consumed this earth already to make it here. But I ask that you look out over the lands from here. You can see just how bad it has become.'"},
[5091]={"Blighted mushrooms gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather blighted water (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blighted water gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather blighted mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blighted sap gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather blighted leaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather bighted leaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fate of the Moulder-wood, Part 8","Gather blighted sap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Viznak about the serum","Return to Viznak with the serum ingredients","Faeron has asked you to help the Rangers to craft a serum against the Pale Blight by assisting Viznak in concocting it.","'The lands here are filled with rot and there is much we must do.\
\
'The blight that has seized this wood is not exactly like the one brewed by Lhaereth, but the two pestilences share some traits. Our work in the north may inform our work here! We believe we can create a serum for this plague. It will not stop its spread, but it may protect the imbiber from the rot's infection.\
\
'If you are ready to get to work, speak with Viznak. Spend not overlong catching up! The sooner we can mix this serum, the sooner we can return to other lands! He will know what should be done as we work towards this potion.'","'Oh, greetings! I knew you would be around here somewhere! Viznak has only to think a thing, and it happens! Just now I was thinking I needed another loyal subject to collect some things, and here you are!\
\
'We are going to make something to help with the bad things here. It helped with the Blight Lady before. This drink needs some more stuff. We saw some good ones that way.'\
\
Viznak points to the north.\
\
'We need some green water, some rocky mushrooms, some leaves that died, and some blood from the trees! Not a problem for you, right? No, no, no, not a problem! You have proven a friend to Viznak before now... once, twice. Is it only twice? Hee hee hee! It seems like more to me, but I am always busy with my rule.\
\
'Now go get that stuff, ${PLAYER}!'","'${PLAYER} returns! I was waiting.'\
\
You give Viznak the items he requested.\
\
'You bring what I needed and you didn't die to the blight! I will get to work right away. It should not take long. Now it is your turn to wait. Hee hee hee!'","You have gathered the requested ingredients for the potion. Return to Viznak in Sul Madásh so he can begin crafting the concoction.","Viznak informed you about the plan for the Pale Blight potion and asked that you gather the needed ingredients from near Sul Madásh."},
[5094]={"'I am eternally grateful to you, ${PLAYER}.'","'Following your departure, I was visited by a powerful emissary of the Rhi Helvarch. As he was the spirit that blessed my union, I asked if there was a way for my people to be freed from this ancient curse. He asked that I choose a champion to go forth and confront my father with what he has done.\
\
'I sent my men to seek out a safe path to Crug Fernvael. I will need to enlist your aid to defeat my father, so our people might be released.\
\
'I will return the amulet that you have mended, as it may aid you when fighting him. Will you travel to Crug Fernvael and defeat him?'","Talk to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary","'With the death of Fernvael, many of the shades in this land are free to move on. The shades that remain have been weakened.\
\
'Your actions bring honour to yourself and your bloodline.'","Talk to Cadelhin at Crug Cadelhin","'My men have returned and have found an entrance to the place where my father was put to rest.\
\
'Please be careful... the shades of his men have been seen there and will attack anyone who might enter therein.'","Cadelhin is at Crug Cadelhin in the Lich Bluffs.\
\
You should talk to Cadelhin when you are ready to travel into Crug Fernvael to confront Cadelhin's father.","Deep within the forgotten barrows of the Lich Bluffs lies Crug Fernvael, the tomb of Cadelhin's father. His defeat might lead to his people's freedom from an ancient curse.","Father of Our Lament","Lhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary in the Lich Bluffs.\
\
Following Fernvael's defeat, many shades have been released from their ancient curse. You should return to Lhudd with the news."},
[5095]={"Collect Ránmald's pendant","Céolstan, son of Aldstan, husband of Ránmald, and father of an unborn child, has been slain by Orcs, sacrificing himself so that the women of Byre Tor could escape.","Céolstan can be found between Byre Tor and the refugees' cave.\
\
You should lay Céolstan to rest.","You ask the wife of Aldstan's son if she wishes to lay a tribute at Céolstan's grave.\
\
Ránmald closes her eyes sadly, and for a few moments seems unable to speak. At last she gives a quiet answer.\
\
'This pendant. He gave it to me, and I have treasured it always. If it is buried with him, it will be a part of me that lies with him....'","The man strains as he looks at you, clearly in pain from his wound.\
\
'It is too late to save me, stranger, but... I am glad you have come. You can help us.\
\
'But first, there is something I would have you do. I cannot... do it myself, and I cannot send Ránmald in her condition. My son lies behind us, dead in the snow, where he fought off Orcs so that these women could steal away.\
\
'Will you lay him to rest? My sword is just here... I will not need it anymore. Lay --lay it with him.'","Ránmald wishes to place a cherished pendant upon her husband's grave","You have buried Céolstan","Ránmald can be found in the refugees' cave in the northern High Knolls.\
\
You should ask Ránmald if there is anything she wishes to bury with her husband.","Aldstan can be found in the refugees' cave in the northern High Knolls.","Father, Husband, Son","Return to Aldstan","Lay Céolstan to rest","Collected Ránmald's pendant","Ránmald's pendant can be found in the refugees' cave in the High Knolls.\
\
You should collect Ránmald's pendant.","'Thank you... friend.'\
\
Aldstan says no more, for he is in great pain.","Céolstan can be found between Byre Tor and the refugees' cave.\
\
You should find Céolstan, and lay him to rest.","Here lies brave Céolstan, who sacrificed himself so that the survivors could escape","Here lies Céolstan, son, husband, and father of Byre Tor survivors.\
\
It is clear from the carnage strewn about him that he was brave and strong. Not many men could have felled so many hale Orcs.\
\
He sacrificed himself so that the women of Byre Tor could escape.","Pick up Aldstan's sword","Ask Ránmald for a tribute to lay at her husband's grave","Collected Aldstan's sword","Find Céolstan's body near Byre Tor","Aldstan's sword sits beside him at the refugees' cave in the High Knolls, north of Byre Tor.\
\
You should collect Aldstan's sword to bury it with his son."},
[5096]={"Tarax is across the Fathomwell from Hûmaz.","Talk to Tarax on the other side of the Fathomwell","'You are back again? Hûmaz thinks I have caught a great number of fish and have them hidden somewhere nearby? It does make sense. After all, he did that very thing himself the other day! I was so furious when I discovered it!\
\
'Yes, this happens a lot. We come to the Fathomwell every morning, and some days he catches more fish than I do, and sometimes I have better luck than he, and often we send a helpful stranger back and forth across the pool to inquire about the other's fortunes. There really is no end to it... at least until the sun goes down, and then we each go back to our homes and it all starts again the next day.\
\
'I suppose I would miss it. But it seems today we are equally-matched in ill fortune.'","Talk to Hûmaz on the other side of the Fathomwell","'Greetings, stranger. I would ask you to keep your voice down, but I do not think that will make a difference today. The fish have not been biting.\
\
'This is the Fathomwell, where water from the bay runs into the great cisterns for use by the folk of Umbar Baharbêl. The fish swim in and become disoriented, which makes for good fishing for me and my companions. Most of the time.\
\
'Perhaps not today. Will you cross to the other side of the Fathomwell and ask Tarax if he is having more good fortune on that side of the pool?'","'How is the fishing over here? Why do you ask?'\
\
Tarax looks at you suspiciously for a considerable length of time, paying no attention to the line he has cast into the Fathomwell. You note that he appears to get not so much as a nibble.\
\
'If Hûmaz thinks he is going to do better than I am, he is better off staying where he is. You go tell him that.'","Fathomwell Fishing","Hûmaz is across the Fathomwell from Tarax.","The Fathomwell cisterns provide water for the rest of the city, but that is no reason for local fishermen to avoid plumbing its depths for their dinners.","'He says I should stay here? Hmm... I don't trust those words.\
\
'Does that mean he is having more luck on that side than I am over here, or does that mean he is looking out for my own interests and believes I must be getting more fish upon my hook on this side?\
\
'Perhaps you will go back to him and see if he is hiding anything from us? Is it possible he caught a great deal of fish and has hidden them somewhere nearby?'","You are reasonably certain that is not the case, but you might talk to Tarax again","'So he has no secret pile of fish today? That is good to know.\
\
'Yes, we have been coming to the Fathomwell for years and years. My father brought me here when I was just a boy, and he would tell me stories of the city and its history. My favourites were always the ones with fighting, like when bloodthirsty Thorongil attacked and set the city aflame. Did you know not even the waters of Fathomwell could put out the fires? They burned for days, my father said.\
\
'Tarax loved those stories too. I had forgotten! We used to fish on the same side of the pool, but at some point we became so competitive that we could not do that any longer. Ah, this is not an uncommon mood for me on days when the fish aren't biting!\
\
'Thank you for helping me as you have. I appreciate it.'"},
[5097]={"Defeated swarming plague-flies","Defeated Agarnaith gore-crow","After completing your survey of the area, you conclude that the animals of Agarnaith are quite dangerous. They all seem to be infected with some sort of disease, driving them into a ravenous frenzy. You will include this note in your scouting report.","Defeat infectious plague-rat","Completado.","Completado","Defeat plagued dire-wolf","Fauna Investigation","Derrota un cuervo sangriento de Agarnaith","Defeat diseased swamp-boar","Defeated plagued dire-wolf","Defeated infectious plague-rat","Since Agarnaith is primarily marshland, it has the potential to contain many dangerous animals. You should investigate before proceeding deeper.","'Since this area is rich in plant-life, it is almost certain animals take refuge here as well. See if you can find any and test your strength against them. Our chances of survival and successfully uncovering the swamp's secrets increase as we learn more about this unusual place.'","Animals can be found in southern Agarnaith.\
\
You should defeat one of each different animal you find.","Defeated diseased swamp-boar","Defeat swarming plague-flies"},
[5099]={"Rascacuevas derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los rascacuevas están destruyendo la tierra con su excavación desenfrenada. Sin alguna forma de reducir su número, temo que el suelo se derrumbe bajo nuestros pies. Incluso los Duramano son conscientes de la amenaza, pero los holgazanes no han hecho nada.\
\
'Bogi, un enano barbiluengo en el Patio de Frerin, pidió que organizara esfuerzos para reducir el número de rascacuevas y ayudar a prevenir más daños.\
\
'Encontrarás rascacuevas a lo largo de la ladera al oeste de las ruinas de Edhelion, rodeando y dentro del Abismo de Plata en la base de la colina. Cuando completes esta tarea, busca a Bogi en el Patio de Frerin, en el centro de la Puerta de Thorin, hacia el oeste.'","'No podemos deshacer el daño causado por los rascacuevas, pero su impacto futuro en las cavernas será mínimo. Gracias, ${PLAYER}, por todo lo que has hecho.'","Derrota rascacuevas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los rascacuevas se encuentran a lo largo de la ladera al oeste de Edhelion, dispersos cerca de la entrada y dentro del Abismo de Plata.\
\
Orodlin te pidió que derrotaras rascacuevas en toda la Puerta de Thorin y entregaras el mensaje a Bogi en el Patio de Frerin.","Habla con Bogi en el Patio de Frerin","Miedo al Colapso","La piedra bajo la Puerta de Thorin está llena de madrigueras de rascacuevas. Si el daño continúa, toda el área podría debilitarse lo suficiente como para colapsar.","'¡Hiciste algo bueno allí!'","Bogi se encuentra en el centro de la Puerta de Thorin, en el Patio de Frerin, al oeste de Edhelion, en el centro del valle.","'Las bestias sin mente cavan y cavan sin preocuparse por el daño que causan. Alguien debe matar a los rascacuevas antes de que hagan más daño.'","'Gracias por tu ayuda con nuestro problema de rascacuevas.'"},
[5100]={"Examine a fallen Corsair","The Corsairs' hideout can be found in north-central Dor-en-Ernil along the mountainside.\
\
You have encountered two Corsairs fleeing south-east of Dol Brannor. You should search the nearby mountainside for their hideout.","Slain Corsairs litter the ground nearby","Miedo a la muerte","Search the cave for more Corsairs","Search for the cave the Corsairs mentioned as they fled","'It would be a far easier task to stop these Corsairs if they had not fled throughout our lands. Those to the north concern me greatly, but not nearly as much as those that fled into the hills.\
\
'The mountainside is rife with small passages and it is likely they hide their numbers within. If we do not rout them now, I can think of few better places to hold for a prolonged conflict.\
\
'Search the mountainside to the north and west of here, ${PLAYER}. Since we have learned much from these Corsairs, I shall return to Linhir and speak with Garvir. When you have learned of their hideout, I trust I shall see you in Linhir once more!'","You have found a cave tucked into the hillside and should explore it further","Corsairs flee nearby, paying you little attention as they pass...","Corsairs have fled into the hills of Dor-en-Ernil, hinting that their forces may be beginning to regroup further from Linhir.","This fallen Corsair curiously bears no wounds. Stranger still, a mixture of surprise and fear are readily apparent in his face, hinting that he and his men were taken unawares by some unknown foe.","Search for the Corsair hideout to the north-west","DNT -- will not be seen","The slain Corsair can be found on the ground of the Corsair cave in north-central Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have found naught but slain Corsairs in the cave and should examine their bodies to determine what has occurred.","The Corsairs' hideout can be found somewhere to the north-west of Hata Khezrat along the mountainside.\
\
Gorroch has asked you to track the Corsairs into the hills in hopes of disrupting them.","The Corsairs' hideout can be found in northern central Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have found the Corsairs' cave and should now search it for any sign of Corsairs."},
[5102]={"'Ah, the pelts! Thank you, my friend. Life can be trying here in Ambarûl and I cannot abide waste. These will help someone greatly when the seasons change.'","Bring the pelts to Turizi","Collected pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Servals and caracals can be found prowling about the rice fields of Ekagar in Ambarûl. You should defeat some and bring their pelts to Turizi.","Fearsome Felines","You have defeated servals and caracals prowling about the rice fields of Ekagar. You should bring their pelts to Turizi behind the farmhouse.","Defeat wild cats and collect their pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have another trouble you could help me with, should you be willing. There are wild cats that live in the untamed lands in the north. At least, that is where they should be living. Of late they have been prowling our fields and frightening my mother as she goes about her work.\
\
'If you are willing to slay some of the vexing animals, let us not be wasteful. Bring me their pelts and I will put them to good use this next winter.'","Turizi has asked you to slay some of the wild cats worrying his mother.","'Of late wild cats have been prowling our fields and frightening my mother. If you are amenable, slay some of them and bring me their pelts.'"},
[5103]={"Habla con el líder del Gremio de Cocineros en Minas Morgul","'¿Cómo va el horneado de pasteles?'","¡El líder del Gremio de Cocineros ha pedido ver cómo se ve tu Pastel de Nueve Estrellas, o a qué sabe!","Ejecuta la receta del Pastel de Nueve Estrellas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Estos pasteles producen el aroma más tentador en el horno, ¿no estás de acuerdo?'","Habla con Aesseledh","'¿Qué podría ser mejor que un Estofado de Siete Estrellas? ¡Un pastel relleno de Estofado de Siete Estrellas, eso es! Agrega queso de cabra picante de los enanos y un poco de salsa de cereza dulce de Rohan y tendrás una comida verdaderamente especial. Querrás dominar esta receta.'","Preparación de festín - Pasteles de Nueve Estrellas","Ejecutaste la receta del Pastel de Nueve Estrellas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las recetas de artesanía que debes crear se pueden encontrar en tu panel de artesanía.\
\
Hornea quince porciones de Pastel de Nueve Estrellas."},
[5104]={"El líder del Gremio de Cocineros te ha pedido que hornees pan de viaje con varios rellenos. ¿Cuál es tu favorito?","Hornea pan de viaje relleno de pollo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Cómo va el horneado?'","Habla con el líder del Gremio de Cocineros en Minas Morgul","Hornea pan de viaje relleno de patata (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pan de viaje horneado de cerdo y fruta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Estos son una bendición en el campo. Llévate algunos contigo la próxima vez que te aventures en lugares peligrosos. Regálale también algunos a tus amigos.'","Las recetas de artesanía que debes crear se pueden encontrar en tu panel de artesanía.\
\
Hornea tres tipos diferentes de pan de viaje, cinco piezas de cada uno.","Preparación de festín - Pan de viaje relleno","Habla con Aesseledh","'Un pan de viaje relleno es como un pastel pequeño pero menos delicioso. Supongo que es mejor comida para viajar. Prueba algunas variaciones de relleno.'","Pan de viaje horneado relleno de patata (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pan de viaje horneado relleno de pollo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hornea pan de viaje de cerdo y fruta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5105]={"Ejecuta la receta de verduras a medio cocer (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ejecutaste la receta de verduras a medio cocer (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con el líder del Gremio de Cocineros en Minas Morgul","Al líder del Gremio de Cocineros le gustaría ver cómo prepararías verduras mixtas.","Preparación de festín - Verduras","'He oído que los granjeros están cultivando diferentes tipos de verduras mezcladas en el campo. ¡Me pregunto si sabrán bien si se comen juntas! Hazme un favor y prepara algunas porciones.'","'¿No tienes algunas verduras para cocinar?'","Las recetas de artesanía que debes crear se pueden encontrar en tu panel de artesanía.\
\
Cocina veinticinco porciones de verduras a medio cocer.","Habla con Aesseledh","'Creo que esta nueva técnica de cultivo es prometedora. Los resultados ciertamente hablan por sí mismos.'"},
[5106]={"Preparación de festín - Masa de pan de viaje","Habla con el líder del Gremio de Cocineros en Minas Morgul","Ejecuta la receta de masa de pan de viaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las recetas de artesanía que debes crear se pueden encontrar en tu panel de artesanía.\
\
Prepara veinticinco porciones de masa de pan de viaje.","Al líder del Gremio de Cocineros le gustaría que intentaras preparar masa de pan de viaje usando una receta antigua.","'¡Bien hecho! Huelen como si estuvieran listas para hornear.'","'¿Has oído? Alguien del Gremio de Eruditos encontró una antigua receta de pan de viaje de los días de la Gran Alianza. Es impresionantemente robusto y no es desagradable de comer, a diferencia del Cram que comen en el norte. Deberías dominar esta receta.'","Ejecutaste la receta de masa de pan de viaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Aesseledh","'${PLAYER}, ¿conseguiste el pan?'"},
[5107]={"'Necesitamos carne de los animales de caza del Bosque Salvaje. Por favor, tráeme carne de jabalí, alce y oso.\
\
'¡Además, he oído hablar de unos terribles árboles andantes en estos bosques! Mi maestra insiste en que, y cito textualmente, “¡los ucornos están podridos hasta la médula, pero su corteza produce el sabor perfecto al ahumar carne y pescado!” Si te encuentras con alguna de estas monstruosas plantas andantes, por favor, tráeme su corteza.\
\
Pisador y yo nos dirigimos al sur. He oído que, al otro lado de esta colina, hay un comerciante que tiene en su poder una especia especial que necesito.'","Habla con Minda Matosos","Los ingredientes para el banquete se pueden encontrar en el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Minda Matosos necesita ayuda para reunir los ingredientes para un gran banquete.","Delicias del Bosque Salvaje completada","Banquete del Bosque Salvaje","'¡No sé cómo podría haberlo hecho sin ti, ${PLAYER}! Bueno, la verdad es que no podría haberlo hecho sin ti. Tendría que bajar la cabeza avergonzada y volver con las manos vacías.\
\
¡Ahora puedo tachar un montón de ingredientes de mi lista! ¡Has salvado el banquete y mi aprendizaje!'","Minda se encuentra en un campamento en el sur del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Minda Matosos.","Carne de oso del Bosque Salvaje conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Consigue carne de oso del Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Consigue carne de jabalí del Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corteza de ucorno del Bosque Salvaje conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Consigue carne de alce del Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Carne de jabalí del Bosque Salvaje conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Tantos platos, tantos ingredientes! ¡Mi futuro como cocinera estará perdido si vuelvo con las manos vacías!'","Carne de alce del Bosque Salvaje conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ya han encontrado el poni y el carro de Minda Matosos, pero ella todavía tiene una tarea que cumplir: reunir los ingredientes para el banquete de su señora."},
[5108]={"Defeat Fangorn Hive-workers under rotting stumps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gredbyg devour and rot trees from below, striking fear into your Huorn companion and threatening Fangorn Forest.","Defeated Fangorn Hive-workers under rotting stumps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Quickbeam's Huorn","As you wander Fangorn Forest, the Huorn travelling with you suddenly seems disturbed. It swiftly strikes a nearby stump with one of its roots causing numerous gredbyg to pour forth. It quickly crushes all of their number, but still appears upset.\
\
You should search rotting stumps for more gredbyg and slay them before they can spread rot deeper into Fangorn.","Gredbyg can be found under rotting stumps throughout southern Fangorn.\
\
The Huorn has expressed naught but contempt for the gredbyg chewing upon the trees of Fangorn. You should defeat them.","DNT -- Players will not see","Feasting on the Forest","You have defeated many gredbyg and stopped them from causing more damage to Fangorn.","The Huorn's anger seems to have subsided, and the gredbyg are no longer able to devour Fangorn from below, at least for the moment."},
[5109]={"Return to Paguri with the pristine feathers","Feather Fetch","Returned to Paguri with the pristine feathers","'Ah, an adventurer. Could I trouble you for some help?\
\
'I am the fletcher here and I am working to build our supply of arrows. We will need all that we can get if we mean to retake Maurûsh.\
\
'If you happen upon any feathers from the creatures here in Urash Dâr, I would be glad to take them off your hands. I do not have the time myself to track them down with the work that must be done.\
\
'Only ones remaining in pristine condition will suffice.'","'These are flawless! I thank you adventurer.\
\
'I will make some fine arrows with these.'","Paguri in Ub Nashir has asked you to gather feathers from nearby birds so that she can replenish her stock of arrows.","Gather pristine feathers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gathered pristine feathers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the pristine feathers back to Paguri in Ub Nishir.","Paguri in Ub Nishir has asked you to gather feathers from birds in Urash Dâr so that she can replenish her stock of arrows."},
[5111]={"Hannar está en Othrikar.\
\
Lograste encontrar al Montaraz que Hannar te pidió buscar, y él te sugirió que buscaras el lugar de anidación de los hendrevail. Debes regresar con Hannar con esta información.","'Los enanos deberían tener cuidado con los hendrevail, pues a menudo son usados como espías por el Enemigo.'","'Si Orthonn en Dehesa del rey puede decirnos algo sobre los hendrevail, quizá tengamos más éxito al enfrentarnos a ellos.'","Habla con Hannar en Othrikar","Habla con Orthonn en Ost Lagoros","Enemigos emplumados","'Ah, sí, los hendrevail. Aves extrañas, violentamente hostiles, incluso con criaturas mucho más grandes que ellas, y muy territoriales. Sin embargo, pueden ser entrenadas. Los hendrevail han sido usados ocasionalmente por orcos y hombres malvados en el pasado, pero en su mayoría su malicia es completamente natural.\
\
¿Así que los barbiluengos de Othrikar temen que sus rivales Duramano estén usando estas aves como espías? Puede que sea cierto. A diferencia de otros halcones y aves rapaces, los hendrevail de las colinas del norte prefieren un lugar de anidación común. Les importa poco sus crías, y probablemente ahí es donde los Duramano recogieron los polluelos para entrenarlos.\
\
Te aconsejo que busques ese lugar de anidación, seguramente en algún rincón apartado de las colinas.'","'A pesar de tu trabajo, parece que hay más hendrevail que nunca en las colinas, y algunos dicen que incluso se han visto en los campamentos de los Duramano.\
\
Sabemos muy poco sobre estas criaturas, aparte de que son aves sucias, malvadas y feroces. Necesitaremos saber más si queremos hacer algo al respecto. Hay un cazador llamado Orthonn que suele recorrer Dehesa del rey y podría saber más sobre criaturas salvajes como Los hendrevail. se Hace llamar montaraz, un tipo extraño. suele encontrarse en un campamento en las viejas Ruinas De ost lagoros, no muy lejos al noroeste de la Granja de gatson, algo al sur y Oeste de othrikar.\
\
Te agradecería que pudieras ir a hablar con él por mí.'","'¿Un lugar de cría, dices? Me pregunto...\
\
Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Cuando descubramos la ubicación de este nido, puede que vuelva a necesitar tu ayuda.'","A pesar de tus esfuerzos, la amenaza de los hendrevail sigue siendo una plaga en las colinas alrededor de Othrikar.","Orthonn está recogiendo hierbas en Dehesa del rey, probablemente en su campamento en las Ruinas De ost lagoros al noroeste de la Granja de gatson, algo al sur y Oeste de othrikar.\
\
Hannar explicó que su gente no sabía lo suficiente sobre los hendrevail como para saber cómo enfrentarse a ellos, ya que cazarlos no Parecía funcionar. te pidió que hablaras con un Cazador llamado orthonn, que podría tener información sobre estas aves."},
[5112]={"'Have you brought the feathers that Amlan requested of you?'","Collect pristine feathers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pristine feathers might be found in the nests of the crebain at Pluvun Gwern, north-east of Echad Saeradan.\
\
Amlan has asked you to collect pristine feathers to trade to the Algraig of Enedwaith.","The Rangers of the Grey Company seek to acquire the good will of the Uch-lûth, the Dunlending clan inhabiting Enedwaith.","'These are the feathers that Amlan requested of you? Good! Then all is nearly in readiness.'","'Aye, ${PLAYER}, I believe these will do well. Bring them to Saeradan...he will know what to do with them.'","Feathers for Friendship","Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith, south-west of Pluvun Gwern.\
\
Amlan told you to take the craban-feathers to Saeradan to be prepared for delivery to the Algraig.","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! It has been long since you rid the Hobbits of Buckland of the threat of the giant. Thanks to you, they may wander the Brandy Hills with little fear.\
\
'Now, I am in need of your aid once more. The Algraig use feathers for bedding and decoration, ${PLAYER}. It may be to our benefit to collect many pristine feathers to bring to them as an offering of peace. Perhaps such an offering will entice them to trade with us.\
\
'Crebain nest at Pluvun Gwern to the north-east of here. Perhaps you may find pristine feathers within their nests. Bring them to Saeradan...the feathers must be of the highest quality.'","'Search the nests of the crebain at Pluvun Gwern, north-east of here, for the feathers we require.'","Collected pristine feathers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the craban-feathers to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan"},
[5113]={"The hill of Cracabor is the highest point in the Wold, and is located just north of the Twickenburg.\
\
You should climb Cracabor and collect feathers from the evil flock that has landed there.","Bring the feathers to Sergeant Tidlac","The hill of Cracabor is covered in spying crebain that intimidate the surrounding lands with their sinister gazes.","Recoge plumas de craban (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The feathers you collected from the crebain will be very useful, ${PLAYER}. We use them for arrows, bedding, and all sorts of things. Better for us to have them than those evil birds.'","Plumas de craban recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Feathers of the Flock","Kill a spying craban","Sergeant Tidlac is keeping watch on the road from the fort of Twickenburg, between Harwick and Floodwend.\
\
You should bring the feathers to Sergeant Tidlac."},
[5114]={"Alguien ha puesto una tarea para recoger plumas en el Bosque Salvaje.","Encontrarás una caja de almacenamiento en el Embarcadero de los Comerciantes o en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Debes guardar las plumas en una caja de almacenamiento.","Plumas del Bosque Salvaje","Plumas recogidas en el Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Coloca las plumas en la caja de almacenamiento","Recoge plumas en el Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En el Bosque Salvaje se pueden encontrar plumas en los pájaros.\
\
Deberías recoger plumas.","El anuncio del tablón dice:\
\
'Se necesita: plumas del Bosque Salvaje para obras y reparaciones. Se recompensará su esfuerzo.'"},
[5116]={"Completa el desafío: Fornost - Espectro de la Sombra","¡Completa el desafío de nivel 2 de Fornost - Espectro de la Sombra para recibir recompensas!","Desafío Fornost - Espectro de la Sombra completado","Completa el desafío de nivel 2 en la instancia Fornost - Espectro de la Sombra","Desafío de la semana: Fornost - Espectro de la Sombra","Completa la instancia de la semana: Fornost - Espectro de la Sombra (nivel máx.)"},
[5121]={"¡Completa el desafío de nivel 2 de las Campanas de Valle para recibir recompensas!","Desafío destacado: Las campanas de Valle","Completa el desafío de nivel 2 en la instancia de las Campanas de Valle.","Completado el desafío de las Campanas de Valle","Completa: Instancia de la semana: Las campanas de Valle (nivel máximo)","Completa: Desafío: Las campanas de Valle"},
[5126]={"Completa: Instancia de la semana: Telarañas Enmarañadas (nivel máximo)","Completa el desafío de nivel 2 en la instancia de las Telarañas Enmarañadas.","Completa: Desafío: Telarañas Enmarañadas","¡Completa el desafío de nivel 2 de las Telarañas Enmarañadas para recibir recompensas!","Desafío de las Telarañas Enmarañadas completado","Desafío destacado: Telarañas Enmarañadas"},
[5219]={"Feed for the Horses","'Well done! We should be stocked for a little while now. Thank you for your help!'","Éogar is found by the stables of the horse-farm.","'The horses are sounding hungry, and I have been told their troughs are running empty. I need to have a stable-hand feed the horses very shortly, or they may get agitated, but the helpers are busy at the moment! Can you please help me start on the task and gather the grain? As soon as you get back with it, a helper should be available to feed them.\
\
'There are many bags and sacks of grain around the farm; some might be empty, but there should be enough full ones. Hurry back with the grain!'","Return to Éogar with the grain","There are many bags and sacks of grain spread around the main buildings of Hengstacer Farm.","Éogar can always use more help on his farm, and today he needs help feeding the horses.","You found grain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The grain was mouldy and unfit for horses.","Find grain in the area (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se te ha acabado el tiempo"},
[5220]={"'Help from outsiders? And you were sent by Roshat? He must be getting truly desperate.\
\
'It's true we could use all the help we can get. Our lures are as good and our hands as quick as ever. It's the trout themselves that have changed. They have turned a pallid, slimy green, afflicted with some terrible disease. We know not why. Some of the hands have taken to calling it the stench, for obvious reasons. We cannot eat or sell any of the fish we catch, it makes any who eat it violently ill.\
\
'I'll be honest with you, moreso than perhaps Roshat was – we really could use your help. We rely on the fish to fill our bellies and our coin pouches. I know Roshat has suspicions about the source of the disease, but he won't trust outsiders unless he sees your value.\
\
'I don't know how to heal our fish, but I know how you could help fill our bellies and perhaps gain his trust. There are crabs to the east of here, along the shore, just beyond the village. They seem to be immune to the stench, at least so far. However, they fight back more than we gentle fisherfolk can handle.\
\
'Would you go to the east and bring us back some crab to feed our people?'","'I am grateful. We are proud folk, but I'm not too proud to admit my people will have full bellies tonight thanks to you. You might want to talk to Elder Roshat again.'","Crab meat collected (${NUMBER}/10)","Umaris has asked for your help feeding the village using the large, fierce crabs south of Khûtra. Perhaps Elder Roshat will see your value once you've helped the village.","Return with crab meat to Umaris","Large crabs can be found to the south-east of Khûtra. Go there and return with crab meat to feed the hungry villagers.","'Please, we have so many who are hungry. The crabs can be found to the east along the shore. Please hurry!'","Collect crab meat (${NUMBER}/10)","Feeding A Village"},
[5222]={"Es extraño que los rascacuevas hayan salido en masa de sus cuevas hacia la luz del sol. Quizás algo los ha impulsado a un frenesí alimenticio.","Frenesí Alimenticio","Reduce el número de rascacuevas en el Bosque de los Trolls Sur, ya que son una amenaza para todos en su estado actual de frenesí.","Derrota rascacuevas en el Bosque de los Trolls Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has matado a muchos rascacuevas en el Bosque de los Trolls Sur y has vuelto a hacer seguro el camino para los viajeros.","DNT -- Will not be seen","Rascacuevas derrotados en el Bosque de los Trolls Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota rascacuevas en el Bosque de los Trolls Sur","Completado","Has derrotado a muchos rascacuevas en el Bosque de los Trolls Sur","Los rascacuevas se encuentran por todo el Bosque de los Trolls Sur, pero especialmente en Ost Dúrgonn, al norte del camino y del campamento de Barachen.\
\
Reduce el número de rascacuevas en el Bosque de los Trolls Sur, ya que son una amenaza para todos en su estado actual de frenesí."},
[5223]={"Aid Bernwyn","'You have done very well, ${PLAYER}. I heard joy echoing through Garsfeld in a way I have not for weeks now.\
\
'Those half-orcs have given us enough trouble - now that the people are secure, let us fall upon our foes!'","Gísil wants you to aid the people of Garsfeld with various tasks that he believes will help restabilise the town.\
\
Agelric and Bernwyn can be found in the centre of Garsfeld, while Gísling can be found inside the mead-hall of Garsfeld.","Aid Agelric","Talk to Gísil","Gísil can be found inside the mead-hall of Garsfeld.","'As I said, the safety of my people is of the utmost importance to me. The Half-orcs are causing far more harm than the damage they do outside the town. With our crops ravaged, it won't be long before our supplies of food begin to run dry.\
\
'There are many among us that require aid - I would ask that you seek out Agelric and Bernwyn, two crofters that have toiled for the good of Garsfeld for many years now. Also, I am certain that my son will have another task for you should you seek him out.\
\
'Speak to them, and know that you may yet bring hope back to Garsfeld.'","Gísil has expressed concern for the folk of Garsfeld. He and his men have kept the invaders at bay, but the crofters are too afraid to return to their work. Gísil hopes you can help the people of Garsfeld by aiding them with various tasks.","Aid Gísling","Feeding Garsfeld"},
[5224]={"Bring the meat back to Ningêna at Sûru","Feeding a Small Army","'Fen-wallowers live in a place east of here that we call Shegdush. If you wouldn't mind doing so, hunting some and bringing back the meat would be helpful.'","Collected fen-wallower meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER}, you return with meat! I will see that it is cured for storage. Thank you!'","Ningêna would like more meat added to their stockpile at Sûru.","Collect fen-wallower meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have hunted fen-wallowers and collected their meat. You should bring it to Ningêna in Sûru.","Shegdush, located east of Sûru, has a sizable wild boar population. You should go there and hunt fen-wallowers for Ningêna.","'I have learned that being a commander is not just planning for battles. Keeping your warriors well-fed is key to victory. A hungry army is less effective and could lead to desertions. We are not low on supplies, but I want to shore up our meat reserves. Fen-wallowers live in a place east of here that we call Shegdush. If you wouldn't mind doing so, hunting some and bringing back the meat would be helpful.'"},
[5225]={"Andreg is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.\
\
You should bring the meat you collected to Andreg.","'${PLAYER}, I know that Saeradan seeks to befriend the Uch-lûth in the hopes of opening trade with them, but we have a more immediate need for provisions. To this end, I would ask a favour of you.\
\
'As we entered the Windfells, we have seen many herds of oxen roaming the wilds. Would you hunt some of these oxen and bring me the meat?\
\
'Be wary, however... the Uch-lûth also maintain herds in this region. You should not harm any domesticated oxen that you find.'","Dun oxen can be found throughout the Windfells.\
\
Andreg has asked you to hunt the dun oxen of the Windfells for meat. He warned you not to harm the domesticated oxen of the Uch-lûth.","Feeding the Company","'We must have provisions, ${PLAYER}... without sufficient rations, we shall be too weakened to do Aragorn any good.'","Collect ox-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Rangers of the Grey Company are running short of provisions and seek ways to supplement their remaining supplies.","Collected ox-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! This will help us greatly, though I fear it will not be quite enough. Nevertheless, you have our thanks.'","Bring ox-meat to Andreg at Echad Saeradan","'We will need plenty of meat, if we are to continue our journey.'"},
[5226]={"'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. This meat will go far in provisioning the Grey Company.'","Andreg is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.\
\
You should bring the ox-meat you collected to Andreg.","The Rangers of the Grey Company are running short of provisions and seek ways to supplement their remaining supplies.","Collect ox-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dun oxen can be found throughout the Windfells.\
\
Andreg has asked you to once more hunt the dun oxen of the Windfells, but warned you not to harm the herds of the Uch-lûth.","'The meat you have provided us thus far will not be enough, ${PLAYER}.'","Feeding the Company -- Repeatable","Collected ox-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There are plenty of oxen in the Windfells, ${PLAYER}... the few we hunt should not harm the livelihood of the Uch-lûth.'","Bring ox-meat to Andreg at Echad Saeradan","'While I feel some remorse for hunting the beasts from which the Uch-lûth draw their herds, our quest is urgent, and we must have provisions to complete it. Therefore, I must ask you to go forth once more and hunt the dun oxen of the Windfells.\
\
'Again, do not harm the domesticated herds of the Uch-lûth. I should hope to avoid angering the Uch-lûth as much as possible.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you accept this quest, you will not be able to take the quest A Matter of Doubt.</rgb>"},
[5227]={"Gerardo Hoyondo está en los corrales de la Granja de Cotonorte.\
\
Gerardo Hoyondo se alegrará de saber que se han llenado los pesebres.","Una de las atracciones principales del mercado agrícola de Cotonorte es su zona para acariciar animales.","Has recogido pienso (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Con los pesebres llenos y las vacas alimentadas, todos los animales están listos para el mercado.'","Derrota musarañas en la Granja de Cotonorte (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has derrotado musarañas en la Granja de Cotonorte (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Sé que las musarañas también tienen que comer, pero sin ese pienso no tenemos vacas, y sin vacas no hay leche, queso, mantequilla, nata....'","Recoge pienso (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Alimentar a las vacas","Has llenado los pesebres (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Los cerdos están lo más felices que haya visto en mucho tiempo. Creo que el barro es el más espeso que he visto nunca. Serán felices en su lodazal.\
\
'Queda un último animal en la granja del que debemos ocuparnos: las vacas. No hay mucho que hacer aparte de traer algo de pienso y llenar los pesebres. Sin embargo, últimamente hemos tenido problemas con el pienso: las musarañas.\
\
'Si pudieras ahuyentar a unas cuantas musarañas mientras recoges el pienso, y luego llenas los pesebres, creo que todos los animales estarán listos para el mercado.'","Las musarañas y los sacos de pienso se encuentran cerca de Gerardo Hoyondo en la Granja de Cotonorte.\
\
Gerardo Hoyondo te ha pedido que recojas los sacos de pienso y ahuyentes a las musarañas que los están robando.","Los pesebres están en los corrales de la Granja de Cotonorte.\
\
Hay que echar el pienso en los pesebres para las vacas.","Habla con Gerardo Hoyondo","'Adelante, echa el pienso en los pesebres para que las vacas puedan comer.'","Llena los pesebres (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[5229]={"Sighild holds out a honey cake.\
\
'Oh, this isn't for you. I apologize if you thought I was giving this honey cake to you, I am just proud of this batch, is all. This is a special, and exceptionally hearty recipe that would keep a fighting dwarf full for a day! Hmm, are you venturing out into battle yourself? Would you take these honey cakes with you and deliver them to the hungry dwarves on the front lines? I would be most thankful!'","Deliver honey cakes to hungry dwarves (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have successfully delivered many of Sighild's honey cakes to hungry dwarves on the front lines of the battlefield. Those brave fighting dwarves will not forget all that you have done to assist in the war effort.","Delivered many honey cakes to hungry dwarves.","Completado","Hungry dwarves can be found on the front lines of the battlefield.\
\
You should deliver honey cakes to hungry dwarves.","Delivered honey cakes to hungry dwarves (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Feeding the Front Line","The Beorning Sighild has prepared a batch of war-time honey cakes to feed those on the front line."},
[5230]={"Puedes encontrar alces por toda la región de Länsi-mâ.\
\
Ríki te ha pedido que ayudes a reabastecer los almacenes de Zigilgund con carne de alce.","Consigue cuartos traseros de alce (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Alimentando a los necesitados","Cuartos traseros de alce conseguidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Excelente! Ya casi puedo saborear esos filetes.\
\
'Pondremos algunos al fuego ahora mismo... ¡ningún enano podrá resistir ese chisporroteo cuando lo oiga! Y el resto irá para raciones de viaje y a nuestros almacenes.\
\
'Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. Se te recordará con cada barriga llena.'","'La minería y los otros trabajos que llevamos a cabo aquí hace que los enanos estén hambrientos, como podrás imaginar.\
\
'Sin embargo, nuestras reservas se están agotando, especialmente desde que una de nuestras líneas de suministro fue atacada y saqueada. Nos queda poco de todo... telas, cerveza, cuero y pieles, hebillas y herrajes... Pero lo peor sin duda es que nos queda muy poca carne.\
\
'La carne de alce se seca, ahúma, congela y cura muy bien, además de servir para cocinar jugosos asados. Tráeme un poco de carne, si puedes. Puedes encontrar alces por todo Länsi-mâ.'","Ríki está preocupado por las escasas provisiones para sus mineros hambrientos.","'¿No puedes encontrar alces? ¿O no se te da bien cazarlos? Me lo merezco por pedir ayuda a un extraño.'","Lleva los cuartos traseros de alce a Ríki en Zigilgund"},
[5231]={"Los osos pueden encontrarse en las tierras salvajes alrededor de Gondamon, especialmente hacia el norte.\
\
Gafí te ha pedido que consigas carne de oso para ayudar a llenar las reservas de Gondamon para los meses venideros.","Reúne patas de carne de oso (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Nuestros cazadores son hábiles, pero la caza de este año ha sido especialmente difícil, entre el frío y los miserables Duramano. Me he quedado corto de provisiones para el invierno que se aproxima.\
\
'Puedes ayudarnos trayendo algo de carne de oso. Hay muchos osos en las tierras salvajes alrededor de Gondamon, especialmente hacia el norte.\
\
'Preservaremos y almacenaremos la carne para los meses venideros.'","Patas de carne de oso reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Abasteciendo el Puesto","Gafí, el proveedor de Gondamon, te ha pedido ayuda para reunir provisiones para el invierno.","'Aún necesitamos esa carne de oso, ${PLAYER}. Deberías poder encontrarla en las tierras salvajes que rodean Gondamon.'","'¡Gracias por traer esta carne de oso! Me aseguraré de que sea debidamente salada y almacenada para los meses de invierno.'","Lleva la carne de oso a Gafí en Gondamon."},
[5232]={"'Hmph, these pigs made me work just to feed them! They'll likely start expecting me to come to them with food, too. I've got to find another way -- when I have less work to do, perhaps.\
\
'Thank you for your aid, traveller.'","Fed pigs (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Mileth","You have fed all the pigs you could find around Glaniath.\
\
You should talk to Mileth.","Mileth has asked you to help her feed the pigs wandering around Glaniath.","'Have you come across any of our pigs, traveller? I have food for them, but they seem more interested in wandering around Glaniath instead!\
\
'I can't afford to keep waiting -- I'm going to start looking for them. If you don't mind helping out, here's some food to feed those stubborn beasts!'","It's meal time for the pigs of Glaniath.","Feeding the Pigs","Feed pigs in Glaniath (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[5233]={"Deliver meals to hungry shipmen in the Sail-haven (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'It is a miracle what we can accomplish now that Balakhôr and the Heirs have been overthrown, but we must not push ourselves too hard too swiftly as we work to build a new Umbar Baharbêl. It is a credit to the work ethic of our shipmen that the Sail-haven looks scarcely different than it did before the War—or the Mutiny, for that matter. As the new master of the sailors' guild, it is my belief that meals should sometimes be provided at the expense of the guild's coffers. Let our shipmen keep their wages for their own!\
\
'To that end, I have prepared a number of meals for hungry shipmen in the Sail-haven, but I simply do not have the time to deliver them myself. If you could deliver them on my behalf and offer some words of encouragement to our shipmen, I would be most grateful.\
\
'What do you say, ${PLAYER}?'","The Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl is filled with skilled shipmen who toil to better the Free City in the aftermath of the Sea-stone Mutiny.","Delivered meals to hungry shipmen in the Sail-haven (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Zemirah at the Sailors' Guild-hall","Feeding the Sail-haven","'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Hopefully, I'll be able to deliver some meals myself in the future, but I'm certain they all appreciated your help as much as I did!'","Hungry shipmen can be found throughout the Sail-haven, especially on its piers and near its canals.\
\
Zemirah has asked you to deliver meals to hungry shipmen in the Sail-haven.","Zemirah can be found at the Sailors' Guild-hall in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
You have delivered meals to many of the shipmen labouring in the Sail-haven. You should return to Zemirah."},
[5235]={"Harvest oranges and defeat zizani at Burukíri.","Grain harvested (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Zilêndu, a farmer in Ambarûl. Zilêndu can be found at Burukíri, an orchard north of Iridír.","Give the harvested grain and oranges to Zilêndu, the Ambarûli farmer.","Harvest grain in the northern field near the orchard in Ambarûl.","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír","'Ah, yes I could use the help, much as it shames me to say it. These legs have borne strides enough for three men. I have been blessed to work this land for many years, but now the years feel much heavier on my bones than they once did. I am glad for the aid.\
\
'You can start by gathering fruit from the orchard. Beware of the zizani - every year they grow fiercer and seemingly larger. Anything you can do to reduce their number would be greatly appreciated. After that there is some grain that is ready for harvesting in the northern field.'","Speak with Zilêndu at Burukíri","Mizâdi has asked you to assist the local Ambarûli in procuring supplies to feed the soldiers gathered in Iridír.","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír.","Give the harvested oranges to Zilêndu, the Ambarûli farmer","Defeat zizani (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am heartened. A queen without an army is just a deluded fool, smitten with false confidence and capricious lies. But this responsibility cuts both ways. I must provide for those under my care. I am grateful to you, for making that responsibility a bit lighter for me this day.\
\
'I know these food-stocks will aid us in our fight against this Bârshud.'","Defeated zizani (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You move with an enviable speed, that much is sure. I will add these to what my farm-hands gathered, and we will distribute them to Iridír on the next waggon. Thank you for your aid. This harvest would have taken us days without it.'","'A hungry army is half-defeated before they take the battlefield. There is plenty of food in the hills of Ambarûl, but with most of the able-bodied taking up arms to defend her, there are few hands left to pick and harvest the fruits of the soil.\
\
'Would you go to the local orchard and help the farmers there gather grain and fruit to feed our army? Every bit helps to keep morale high and minds sharp, ${PLAYER}.'","Harvest oranges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Feeding the War Effort","Harvested oranges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Harvest grain in the northern field for Zilêndu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5236]={"Fell Experiments","Search the testing camp","'Welcome back, friend. What have you discovered?'","An Angmarim tent!","Search for more clues","Find Mother Amma in Hagbuth","You found a journal!","You found a torn fragment of paper","Busca pistas","Someone has been experimenting on the Wargs of Clovengap and creating even more dangerous abominations.","Mother Amma is in Hagbuth, in south-eastern Clovengap.\
\
You found a fragment of torn paper and a journal detailing sarrowstones experiments. You should bring the journal and paper fragment to Mother Amma.","'As I suspected, the crystals you collected are different from those we saw in Elderslade. We must uncover this new weaver of fell magic who has been enhancing the sarrowstones and using them to create these terrible beasts.\
\
'See if you can find the location where the Wargs are being enchanted. One of the scouts said she saw cages in the tiers above their dens. Search for anything that might help us discover who is behind these abominations. I will meet you in Hagbuth, on the upper tier across the river.'","The Angmarim camp is in south-west Clovengap.\
\
You have discovered an Angmarim camp where a sorceress is conducting experiments on the local Wargs.","Search for the testing site","Warg dens can be found in western Clovengap.\
\
Mother Amma has asked for you search for clues around the Warg dens.","More cages and Angmarim!","A cage! You must be close!","Defeat the Angmarim sorceress","Clues can be found in the upper tiers of south-west Clovengap.\
\
You should continue to look for clues as to how the crystal-encrusted Wargs are being created."},
[5238]={"Habla con Hartrim","Aguasombrías derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los espíritus del Enemigo incluso acechan las aguas de Agamaur.'","'Dannasen dijo que las mismas aguas de Agamaur se levantaron contra ellos y los rechazaron en tiempos antiguos. Desde entonces, él y sus hermanos han anhelado descansar, pero se les ha negado esa posibilidad. Quizás podamos ayudarles...'","'¡Eres una verdadera bendición en estos tiempos difíciles, ${CLASS}!'","'Habla con Hartrim... él te dirá lo que debes hacer.'","Espíritus caídos","Derrota Aguasombrías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Aunque lo temo, creo que el espíritu de nuestro campamento en Agamaur dice la verdad. Hay cosas antiguas y malignas en esta tierra.\
\
'Detrás de estos muros encontrarás espíritus caídos que toman la forma del agua que inunda esta tierra con su corrupción eterna. El espíritu, Dannasen, me dijo que librar a la tierra de estas criaturas podría ayudar a restaurar el orden natural.\
\
'Encontrarás espíritus por toda esta zona e incluso dentro de los límites de la fortaleza y el arboreto, aunque creo que también podrías encontrarlos por las primeras ruinas de Garth Agarwen.'","'¡Tu coraje nos da fuerza!'","'Si una criatura de carne y hueso puede enfrentarse a los aguasoscuras, quizás los espíritus de Arthedain también puedan hacerlo.'","Las mismas aguas de Agamaur se han levantado para proteger a Ivar y a la Doncella Roja, animadas por los espíritus caídos de Morgoth que han regresado del más allá.","'El terror de las Aguasombrías ha sido derrotado... te estamos en deuda, ${PLAYER}.'","Las Aguasombrías se encuentran en la zona de Garth Agarwen. \
\
Hartrim te ha pedido que le ayudes a apaciguar al espíritu de Agamaur, Dannasen, destruyendo los espíritus caídos que corrompen las tierras de Garth Agarwen.","'${PLAYER}, este servicio es realmente grande. Si las sombras son capaces de levantar su maldición, la tierra podrá comenzar a sanar.\
\
'Este fue un primer paso crucial para que eso sucediera. Gracias.'","'¡Nuestra hora ha llegado, y nuestra victoria no se retrasará más, gracias a ti, ${RACE}!'","Hartrim se encuentra en la entrada de la zona de Agamaur llamada Garth Agarwen.\
\
Los aguasoscuras tienen el poder de infundir miedo incluso en los espectros malditos de Arthedain, impidiéndoles avanzar hacia Garth Agarwen y cumplir su maldición. A petición de Hartrim, fuiste a destruirlas y tuviste cierto éxito. Deberías volver con Hartrim para informarle de tu victoria.","'¡Gracias a ti, ${PLAYER}, nuestra libertad está cerca!'","'¿Nos temes? No lo hagas; no hay nada que temer. Hemos habitado demasiado tiempo en esta Tierra Media, demasiado tiempo sin nuestro merecido descanso. Y sin embargo, aquí seguimos, encadenados por una deuda impaga, un juramento incumplido. ¿Nos prestarías tu ayuda?\
\
'En Garth Agarwen, los espíritus caídos agitan las aguas de Agamaur y toman forma. Muchos son espíritus venidos del más allá, como los que animan a los tumularios, pero los peores son los espíritus malditos de los Hombres mortales, Hombres de Númenor que cometieron un gran acto de maldad contra los Valar antes de la caída de Númenor y fueron maldecidos por los propios Valar.\
\
'¿Nos ayudarías destruyendo estos aguasoscuras?'"},
[5239]={"Reúne piedras rúnicas de los invocadores kergrim dentro de las Tumbas de Khâb Ishil.","Derrota a Zâkrat el Susurrador","Piedras rúnicas de los invocadores kergrim reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Zâkrat el Susurrador, líder de los kergrim, ataca a aquellos que han frustrado sus planes.","'Ahora que has derrotado a Zâkrat el Susurrador, esta zona ya no representa una amenaza para la población. Gracias.'","Derrota a los espíritus crueles que han sido invocados en las Tumbas de Khâb Ishil.","Reune las piedras rúnicas de los invocadores kergrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cuando el último espíritu cruel cae, Zâkrat el Susurrador entra en las Tumbas de Khâb Ishil y te desafía","Derrota a los espíritus crueles que se acercan","Disipados los escudos de sombra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Disipa los escudos de sombra que protegen los altares de ritual (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Invocaciones infames","Los kergrim no solo profanan las tumbas de Khâb Ishil, sino que también las utilizan para invocar espíritus crueles al mundo.\
\
Encuentra una forma de interrumpir el ritual y acabar con esta amenaza.","Zâkrat el Susurrador derrotado","Disipa los escudos de sombra que protegen los altares de ritual con las piedras rúnicas que has reunido dentro de las Tumbas de Khâb Ishil."},
[5240]={"Talk to Lhucu at her hut","'With the banners removed from the village below, we have sent a clear message to my father's forces: their tyranny shall not be tolerated!'","Lhucu is at her hut, north of Lhan Bach.\
\
You should return to Lhucu and let her know that the standards have been destroyed.","'Have you torn down my father's banners?'","Tear down Dievlig banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tore down Dievlig banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'From this vantage point, I can see new standards flying in the valley below. These standards seem to indicate that my father may be seeking new allies to renew his fight.\
\
'Will you go down to Lhan Bach and tear down these standards? That, perhaps, will embolden the people against my father's tyranny.'","Trehéarn Brenin's banners fly in Lhan Bach, south of Lhucu's hut.\
\
Lhucu has asked you to tear down her father's standards that now hang throughout the village of Lhan Bach.","Heartened by the potential allegiance of the elders of Lhan Bach, Lhucu proposes a plan to liberate the village.","Fell the Banners"},
[5241]={"Fell the Fallen","Sâd Doldúr lies to the south of Barad Angol.\
\
Himeinior has asked you to find and dispatch several fell spirits near Sâd Doldúr and collect tokens of their allegiance.","'Dispatch several fell spirits near Sâd Doldúr and collect tokens of their allegiance, then return them to me.'","'Scattered among the ruins below, fell spirits of Morgoth have risen and now haunt the grounds. These creatures have begun appearing in staggeringly large numbers near Sâd Doldúr.\
\
'Could you travel to the ruins below and banish these creatures? I am sure you may find some token of their allegiance wherever they fall. Bring me some of these, as well, to prove your success.\
\
'The spirits are found in great number outside of Sâd Doldúr below. Return to me when you have completed your task.'","Collected ancient coins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Among the ruins on the eastern border of the Ashenslades, fell spirits from beyond the Void have risen and wander the area.","'The number of fell spirits in the area and the look of these coins leads me to believe that the foul sorcerer Orthadban in Sâd Doldúr may have a hand in this matter.\
\
'Thank you for retrieving these coins... perhaps they will shed some light on the true cause of the appearance of so many fell spirits in the Ashenslades.'","Collect ancient coins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Himeinior","Himeinior is at Barad Angol, north and up the mountain from Sâd Doldúr.\
\
You should return to Himeinior with the tokens you collected from the fell spirits of Sâd Doldúr.","Derrota a los espíritus malvados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Espíritus malignos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5243]={"'¿Así que Elsie te envía? ¡Qué alegría!\
\
'Bueno, tuvimos un encontronazo con los orcos... y tuvimos suerte de haber escapado con vida, ¡vaya que sí! Pero nuestro carro... bueno, ¡no salió tan bien parado, como puedes ver!\
\
'No importa cuántos árboles talemos, ¡si no arreglamos el carro no podremos llevarlos de vuelta a Puente de Caballetes!'","'La otra cosa necesaria para las barricadas es madera. En el pasado hubiéramos talado árboles en el Nan Wathren cuando necesitaramos madera, pero ahora los orcos acechan por allí.\
\
'Estábamos tan desesperados por conseguir madera que mi marido, Mattie, y mi hermano, Noll Tobbit, se arriesgaron a dejar Puente de Caballetes y fueron hacia el norte por el mismo Camino Verde en busca de árboles que talar. Ha pasado demasiado desde que supe por última vez de ellos, y me preocupa que algo terrible haya ocurrido.\
\
'¿Podrías buscarlos en el Camino Verde hacia el norte? No puedo soportar pensar que algo malo les haya ocurrido.'","Mattie Bosquerudo y Noll Tobbit deben encontrarse en algún lugar del Camino Verde al norte de Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Elsie te ha dicho que no ha tenido noticias ni de su marido Mattie o de Noll Tobbit, su hermano, desde que se marcharon y te ha pedido que los busques.","'Mattie y Noll dijeron que se dirigían al norte por el Camino Verde, ¡así que probablemente los encuentres allí! ¡Estoy muy preocupada de que algo terrible les haya ocurrido!'","Elsie Bosquerudo te ha dicho que su marido, Mattie, y su hermano, Noll, dejaron Puente de Caballetes para ir en busca de árboles que talar para las barricadas.","Talando árboles"},
[5244]={"You should tell Miruhir that you have finished repairing the fence.\
\
Miruhir can be found in Iáphel.","Miruhir has asked you to repair fences around a section of vineyard in Iáphel.\
\
The broken fences can be found on the western hill of Iáphel.","Talk to Miruhir","'Recent storms have damaged sections of fence around the vineyard. Animals have taken advantage of these gaps to sneak onto the grounds and feast on the fruit. One time a sheep managed to get into the wine. I spent the next hour watching an apologetic shepherd coax the drunk critter back to the rest of the flock. As amusing as that was, it's probably for the best that it doesn't happen again.'","Fence Repair","Repaired sections of fence (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","There are broken sections of fence in Iáphel that need mending.","Repair sections of fence (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you. Another thing off my mind.'"},
[5245]={"The Fang of Shadows stalks the area outside the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras.\
\
Amarion has asked you to hunt the Fang of Shadows, leader of the Shadow-wolves in the Black Dens.","'The Fang of Shadows is a leader among the Shadow-wolves...hunt him and defeat him, ${PLAYER}.'","Among the fell spirits which have taken form as Shadow-wolves, there is one that is more dangerous than all the rest.","Defeat the Fang of Shadows","You have defeated the Fang of Shadows","Amarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.\
\
You should speak with Amarion and let him know that you have defeated the Fang of Shadows, but that the power of the Black Dens seems unbroken.","Talk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras","'So, even with the defeat of the Fang of Shadows, we still seem no closer to breaking the spell that binds these terrible spirits.\
\
'Well, at least that one shall not hunt today, though I suspect we shall see it again before long. My thanks for your efforts...and hopefully a short respite.'","'Something particularly evil stalks this corner of Enedwaith. We have no idea how they came here, but the wolves of the Black Dens are altogether unnatural. They look like wolves and seem to behave as such, but they are not mortal creatures. They are fell spirits that stalk and hunt Men.\
\
'Nor are they aimless -- they are seeking something. The locals say that some were seen in Eregion weeks ago, ranging far and wide in search of their prey, but then they left and returned here to their dens. Only when we of the Dúnedain came did they emerge and resume their hunt...for us it now seems. They can be slain as any wolf might be, but with death they melt away like a shadow in the light of the noon sun.\
\
'When you rescued me I was hunting one of their kind that seemed unique -- a great feral shadow that dominated the others. It was my hope that should this one be slain, then whatever power binds them here would be broken -- but as you know, I became the hunted instead and am still too injured to try my hand at it again. Would you take up my hunt? I cannot say what will come of it, but the passage of our brethren through Enedwaith would be considerably simpler without packs of Shadow-wolves nipping at our flanks the whole way.'","Feral Shadow"},
[5246]={"'Has detenido la malvada máquina del Caldero de la Muerte, has frenado el suministro de dinero a las Quebradas del Norte, y has puesto fin al terror de Deluches, ¡pero aun así los Muertos se alzan! Temo que esto sea obra del temido hechicero, el señor Ferndúr. Has reunido aliados y nos has ayudado a frenar la propagación de los Muertos. Sin embargo, derrotar a Ferndúr no es tarea pequeña. Si deseas desafiar a este funesto maestro de la muerte, debes reunir una fuerza aún mayor.\
\
'Creo que Ferndúr está más preocupado por la invocación de los espíritus malignos que se usan para animar los cuerpos tambaleantes de los muertos, que por los propios tumularios. Debes regresar a la isla maldita en Imlad Balchorth, encontrar el lugar donde los espíritus malignos se agolpan y destruirlos. Destrúyelos a todos, y quizá Ferndúr aparezca, pues debe saber cuando sus espíritus invocados son desterrados.\
\
'Ten cuidado, pues esta amenaza puede ser la más grave hasta ahora, enfrentada en la oscuridad de Angmar, un mal monstruoso cuyo único superior en el Norte se encuentra en la temida ciudadela de Carn Dûm misma.'","Habla con Throst","'Realmente has realizado una hazaña digna de los grandes relatos de épocas pasadas. Puede que pase mucho tiempo antes de que Imlad Balchorth sea purificado de su antigua maldad, pero con un solo golpe has quebrado uno de los principales pilares que sostienen la vil fuerza de Angmar.\
\
'Te saludo.'","Ferndúr el Virulento","Has encontrado la guarida de Ferndúr","'¡El asesino de Ferndúr! ¡Honraré tu nombre entre los Pueblos Libres!'","Throst cree que el hechicero Ferndúr se preocupa por los espíritus malignos que habitan la zona no muy lejos del Caldero de la Muerte.","'¡Encuentra a los espíritus malignos, y eventualmente encontrarás a su maestro!'","Throst está de vuelta en Gath Forthnir, al este de la guarida de Ferndúr.\
\
Con Ferndúr muerto, debes regresar a Throst para contarle la historia de tus hazañas.","Haz salir y derrota a Ferndúr","Hay espíritus malignos en una zona en ruinas no muy lejos del Caldero de la Muerte, en la isla central de Imlad Balchorth.\
\
Ferndúr debe ser destruido para dispersar la amenaza maligna en esta tierra maldita."},
[5250]={"Habla con Gredlan Artemisa.","'Enséñale este boleto a Avery y sabrá que has encontrado un comprador para las flores.'","Habla con Gredlan Artemisa","Una vez al día, Gredlan Artemisa puede darte un boleto del festival.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Boleto del festival","'Avery necesita ayuda recogiendo flores, pero es muy selectivo sobre a quién le permite ayudarle. Quiere que esa persona ha preparado un lugar donde poner las flores. Dime si te interesaría recibir un boleto que le demuestre que hemos hablado.'"},
[5252]={"'No puedo entender las marcas de estos anillos de defensa, ${PLAYER}, pero siento que deben tener algún significado. Conozco a alguien que podría ser capaz de leer su significado, pero está lejos de aquí y la amenaza de los gigantes y los mamuts está mucho más cerca.\
\
Sin embargo, si te mueves con rapidez y eliges una montura veloz para ayudarte en tu misión, podrías alcanzar a la persona de la que hablo y obtener su consejo. Hablo de Gailthin la Elfa, que fue emisaria del Maestro Elrond ante los gigantes. Era una de las pocas personas a las que parecían respetar. Fue enviada al Ered Luin para ocuparse de los problemas de esa región y aún no ha regresado.\
\
He oído que debía reunirse con el capitán de la ciudad enana de Gondamon, en las tierras bajas del Ered Luin. Búscala y muéstrale los anillos de defensa que has arrancado a los grandes mamuts. ¡Su trato con los gigantes podría darle alguna idea sobre lo que podrían significar sus marcas!'","Gailthin se encuentra en la ciudad enana de Gondamon, en las tierras bajas de Ered Luin.\
\
Golhador te ha pedido que muestres los anillos de defensa al emisario Gailthin.","Gailthin la Elfa fue emisaria ante los gigantes en tiempos más felices, y es una de las pocas personas que podría entender el significado de los anillos de defensa que has recuperado.","Pocos se atreven","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Ha pasado mucho tiempo desde que estuve en Imladris y debo decirte que lo he echado de menos.\
\
¿Has quitado estos anillos de las defensas de los mamuts? Debes ser realmente poderoso para haberlo hecho, ¡un valiente ${RACE}, sin igual! Reconozco estos símbolos y sé lo que son: marcas de propiedad.\
\
Puedo decirte los nombres de los gigantes que han tomado a estos mamuts como aliados. Solo ellos pueden incitar a los mamuts a actuar contra nosotros; solo espero que mi conocimiento pueda ayudarte a eliminar esta amenaza antes de que sea demasiado tarde.'","Lleva los anillos de defensa a Gailthin"},
[5254]={"Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.\
\
You should speak with Tolwin.","Tolwin has asked you to mitigate the damage done to crops north of Cirthost by putting out fires in the fields, then collect any supplies that haven't been burned by the enemy.","Supplies can be found around the farm houses in Parth Lisc.\
\
Now that the fires are dealt with, you should recover any supplies from the farm.","Put out fires in the fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the supplies for Tolwin","'I am glad to hear that fires will not spread. It is a shame that the farm is lost. I know that we can not save all of Talath Anor. Let us hope that Crithost will stay strong though.'","'The look-out in Crithost's tower has seen fires in the farmlands north of here. I suspect there is no saving Parth Lisc's crops, but many are concerned that the fires will spread if left unchecked. Ceveneth says that a small shift in the wind is all it would take.\
\
'If you are heading to Parth Lisc, please douse the flames. I do not want all of this peaceful land to burn. If you happen to spy any supplies on the farm, salvage them as this village desperately needs additional supplies.'","You've gathered water to put out the fires!","Suministros recuperados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fields Aflame","Fires can be found in the fields near Parth Lisc.\
\
You should put out fires in the fields.","Recover supplies from Parth Lisc (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5255]={"'Oh my, thank you! I will feel much safer doing my work now. It isn't much, but take this with my gratitude.'","Talk to Sûlmur","Defeat zizani (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat crocodiles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated crocodiles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sûlmur has offered you a reward for defeating crocodiles and zizani, what the locals call Neekers, in the papyrus fields at Mehêtur in Ambarûl.","'The reeds grow easily here, but one must tread carefully in the bog. There is no small amount of crocodiles and zizani among the reeds.  Verily, they seem to be more hostile of late. It is concerning. Are you a ${CLASS}? If you are apt to fighting, I would not complain if you were to rid me of the beasts! I can offer you a small reward for your trouble.'","You have defeated crocodiles and zizani in the papyrus fields. You should return to Sûlmur north-east of the fields.","Fields of Danger","Sûlmur has trouble with aggressive crocodiles and Neekers lurking among the papyrus reeds.","'If you are apt to fighting, I would not complain if you were to rid me of the crocodiles and zizani in the marshes here in Mehêtur. I can offer you a small reward for your trouble.'","Defeated zizani (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5256]={"Fields of Uncertainty","Aided the farmers of Faldham (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Aid the farmers of Faldham (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Return to Osin in Faldham","Farmers can be found all around the Mead Hall of Faldham, at their individual farmsteads.\
\
Osin has asked you to seek the various farmers around Faldham and to lend them what aid you can.","'Hail, friend. Thane Elfmar has given word that the Elfward are to prepare their steeds and equipment for what will be a dangerous assault against our home. I must keep focused upon this task, yet I cannot help but be concerned for the people of Faldham.\
\
'The crofters are terribly unready for the coming siege. Without proper preparation, many are certain to die fighting for their land and home. May I entrust you with aiding these people of merit? Lend them your skill, and I will see that you are rewarded for your trouble.'","Osin has concerned himself with the unreadiness of the crofters around Faldham for the impending siege. He prepares his body for battle, while his mind lingers on the affairs of the crofters.","'Knowing that the people of Faldham will be ready for what comes is of great assurance to me. There are few men who would go to such great lengths to aid us. It is my pleasure to call you friend, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'My mind will now rest solely upon thoughts of victory in the coming battle.'","Osin prepares outside the Mead Hall at the centre of Faldham.\
\
The farmer's troubles have been put to rest, and Osin may now focus on his own problems.","'The crofters can be found at their farmsteads, located around Faldham. Déorun resides at the small home at the centre of the village. Thurgyr lives just south of the Mead Hall. Haligmar dwells to the east, neighbouring Sahard's farm. Lastly, Enswith can be found at the north end of town.'"},
[5257]={"Fiendish Foes","Ingi is at Ost Ringdyr, south of Grothum.\
\
With the goblins dispatched, the time has come to return to Ingi.","Lieutenant Ingi explained that the Snowreap goblins are the same who inhabit Goblin-town and the bulk of the Misty Mountains. He knows that they are an ally to Angmar and wants to see their numbers culled.","There are Snowreap-guards and sappers at Grothum, north of Ost Ringdyr.\
\
Lieutenant Ingi wishes to cull the Snowreap goblins from the Ettenmoors and weaken the forces which Angmar can bring to bear against the Free Peoples.","'A glorious victory for the Free Peoples! Those little beasts deserve no better.\
\
'Your work is far from done, but this is a victory well-earned. Take this with my thanks. Remember that Quartermaster Ash will furnish you a key in exchange for a fair number of these.'","'In an age long past, the Misty Mountains were home to many of my kin. Now they crawl with goblins in all places save Moria where Durin's folk still hold the darkness at bay.\
\
'The goblins in the north, at Grothum their accursed village, are the same that dwell in the place called Goblin-town. These savage little beasts are vile and cruel fiends, desiring only to serve the Dark Lord and the will of all evil manner. We can do our part, however, and crush them. Drive them back into their mountain halls and pursue them until there is nowhere else for them to flee.\
\
'Go north, friend. North to where the hills take on the dark colour of mountain slate. You will find their accursed village. Find the guards and sappers there and put an end to their fiendish ways.'","'See this done, friend. Goblins are among the cruelest creatures in these hills. We'll be better served with them driven far from these lands.'"},
[5268]={"Permanece con el caballo y usa la emote correcta","'¡Bien hecho! El caballo regresó justo antes que tú, y se lo ve mucho más tranquilo.'","Cuéntale a Éogar lo sucedido","El caballo se encuentra afuera, en los Campos de Caballos.","Los caballos pueden ser entrenados y responden a distintos tonos de voz o señales.","'El nuevo caballo que llegó contigo desde Combe parece inquieto, y deberías pasar algo de tiempo con él. Ve a los Campos de Caballos y mira qué puedes hacer.'","Luchar o Huir — Repetible"},
[5269]={"The second freebooter you spoke to isn't interested in fighting. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.\
\
Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.","'Hello--oooh!' \
\
The woman's greeting is interrupted by a yawn. \
\
'Sorry about that. I had coffee too late in the day yesterday. I went to sleep late and am still waking up.'\
\
Anyâmat shares her desire to be a shanty-man, and the sleepy freebooter's lips curl into a smirk.\
\
'If it is inspiration for songs you seek, I can tell you about my own travels on the sea.'\
\
Anyâmat quickly agrees, and the sleepy freebooter proceeds to tell the most bawdy and violent tales one could tell. By the end of the stories, Anyâmat is frozen stiff by shock.\
\
She thanks the woman for her time, and the two of you beat a hasty retreat.","Make friends (2/4)","'Why don't we start by challenging some freebooters to a fight? Nothing speaks to rugged life at sea like pointless brawling!'","'This is not going how I expected. Maybe we should give up on trying to pick a fight and make friends instead.'","The third freebooter gave you and Anyâmat some grilled fish. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.\
\
Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.","Challenge freebooters (0/8)","Anyâmat rushes to your side","The second freebooter you spoke to wasn't interested in fighting. Anyâmat has decided to change strategies and wants to make friends with these freebooters instead.\
\
Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.","Anyâmat wants to make friends with all four freebooters on this little island.\
\
Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.","The first freebooter you spoke to wasn't interested in fighting. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.\
\
Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzir.","'Ah, such lovely weather we have been enjoying as of late. It makes me want to sing!'\
\
The freebooter strikes up a joyful song. Anyâmat doesn't know the words, but she harmonizes beautifully with the man. She may not have success writing lyrics, but doesn't lack for singing talent.","'I know we look like rough folk, but that is what happens when you spend all day in the sun and having your face chapped by salty sea air!'\
\
He laughs, no, guffaws at himself.\
\
'Are you hungry? The sea has been generous and there is plenty of food to share.'","Make friends (4/4)\
Talk to Anyâmat","Make friends (3/4)\
Talk to Anyâmat","Defeat freebooters (0/8)","Anyâmat has made unexpected friends with the freebooters she was intending to instigate! Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.\
\
Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.","Fightin' Freebooters","'Well that didn't go as I expected,' Anyâmat says as she sips from the offered cup. 'Free tea though. Maybe we can challenge one of the other people here?'","Make friends (3/4)","'As lovely as this has been, I do think a real sailor should get into a scrap. If these fine folk won't fight with us, I have heard rumours of a strange creature we could go bother....'","Anyâmat speaks through a mouthful of grilled fish.\
\
'I should go around talking to strangers more often! Instead of fighting you they give you free tea and fish and sing with you. I really like these folks. Come, let's meet the last of their company.'","The first freebooter you spoke to isn't interested in fighting. Try challenging one of her friends.\
\
Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.","'A fight? Now why would I do that? I have only just met you! Come, join me and my friends for some tea.'","Anyâmat thinks it would be a great idea to pick fights with random freebooters so that she might experience the rough and tumble life of a sailor.\
\
Willing freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.","Anyâmat harbours aspirations of being a great shanty-man.","Talk to Anyâmat"},
[5270]={"${CLASS},\
\
En el norte, más allá del Ram Dúath, hay un campamento de montañeses que llevan años libres del dominio de Angmar. Mi líder ha instruido a algunos de estos hombres, pero necesitamos ayuda.\
\
Búscame en Aughaire, el campamento en el borde norte del Ram Dúath. Estoy en una tienda dentro de un círculo de piedras.\
\
Corunir","Habla con Corunir en Aughaire","Una carta de un Montaraz oculto en el norte, entre un grupo de montañeses que han rechazado el yugo de Angmar, indica que necesitan ayuda más allá del Ram Dúath.","Aughaire es un campamento de montañeses, al norte a través del Ram Dúath.\
\
La carta de Corunir solicita ayuda para los guerreros que resisten contra los opresores Angmarim.","Luchando contra la Opresión","'Me alegra verte.\
\
'Deberías relacionarte con la gente de aquí; no te rehuirán. Hay mucho por hacer en este lugar, y estarán agradecidos por cualquier ayuda que puedas brindar. Este sitio necesita auxilio desesperadamente.'"},
[5272]={"'¡Ese lagarto debe ser eliminado antes de que nos mate a todos!'","'He hervido la baba y la he combinado con varias hierbas para crear un polvo potente. Huele muy apetitoso, pero es un poderoso veneno.\
\
'Espolvoréalo sobre la comida del lagarto en el Abismo Hundido. En algún momento, Crestapiedra debería venir a darse un festín.\
\
'Una vez que esté debilitado, deberías poder derrotarlo.'","Un poderoso lagarto ha estado matando mensajeros enanos. Gyrgir desea que atraigas al lagarto y lo elimines.","'¡El gran lagarto ha muerto, gracias a ti! Recordaré tu valentía.'","Derrota a Crestapiedra","Habla con Gyrgir en Hulwul-nefekh","Luchando contra el limo con limo","La comida del lagarto se encuentra en el Abismo Hundido, al oeste de Hulwul-nefekh.\
\
Gyrgir dice que un poderoso lagarto, Crestapiedra, a menudo se alimenta de cadáveres de grodbogs. Ha elaborado un poderoso veneno para espolvorear sobre la comida. Una vez que Crestapiedra lo coma, Gyrgir cree que tendrás una oportunidad de derrotarlo.","Gyrgir se encuentra en Hulwul-nefekh, al este del Abismo Hundido.\
\
Gyrgir estará encantado de saber que su veneno funcionó y que Crestapiedra no devorará más enanos.","Derrotaste a Crestapiedra","Envenena la comida","'Así que el gran lagarto ha caído. Mis hermanos están vengados...\
\
'Esta noticia me llena de alegría. Asegurarnos de que nuestras rutas de viaje estén despejadas y abiertas es de vital importancia, y esto es un paso en la dirección correcta.'"},
[5273]={"Ringlor y el resto de los Dúnedain están luchando una batalla perdida contra los Angmarim que han tomado Annúminas.","Luchando en las calles","'Annúminas está en la orilla suroeste del lago Nenuial, ${PLAYER}. ¡Te animo a tus aliados y a ti a que os unáis a la batalla contra los Angmarim en las calles!'","'Grandes son tus hazañas en Annúminas, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}.'","Los Angmarim pueden encontrarse por todas partes en las calles de Annúminas, en la orilla suroeste del lago Nenuial.\
\
Ringlor espera que prestando tu ayuda en el combate, puedas ayudar a darle la vuelta a la batalla por Annúminas.","'¡Tu saga contra los Angmarim no deja de crecer, ${PLAYER}!'","Derrota Angmarim en Annúminas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Gracias por tus esfuerzos, ${PLAYER}! ¡Cada tajo de espada, embate de vara y disparo de arco que encuentra su objetivo asegura que habrá menos Angmarim que luchar mañana!\
\
'¡Annúminas será nuestro de nuevo, y los Angmarim serán completamente derrotados! ¡Lo juro!'","Angmarim derrotados en Annúminas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Mis hermanos están luchando una batalla perdida entre los muros de Annúminas, ${PLAYER}. ¡A menos que algo cambie, perderemos la ciudad ante Angmar para siempre!\
\
'Pero tus aliados y tú podríais marcar la diferencia. Derrota a los Angmarim dondequiera que los encuentres dentro de Annúminas, en la orilla suroeste del lago Nenuial, ¡y quizá las cosas cambien a mejor!\
\
'La batalla se extiende por las calles de la ciudad en cada nivel, y los Angmarim nos hacen retroceder a la menor oportunidad. ¡Hagamos que prueben el sabor de la derrota, ${PLAYER}!'","Ringlor está en el campamento de Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
El Montaraz Ringlor te ha pedido que te unas a la batalla contra los Angmarim en la ciudad de Annúminas, y tomes parte en la refriega. Ahora deberías volver con la noticia de tus victorias."},
[5274]={"'Lo has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}, ¡pero esto es solo el comienzo! Tu relato de valentía contra las arañas de los Valles Trenzados me ha animado, pero también contiene noticias que me preocupan. Hay más arañas en los Valles Trenzados de lo que sospechaba.\
\
'Y sin embargo, creo que esto podría sernos de gran ayuda. Si estoy en lo cierto, podríamos usar su gran número a nuestro favor. ¡Debemos averiguarlo, y rápido!'","Thoroniel se encuentra en el Bosque de los Trolls Norte, justo al sur de los Valles Trenzados, en la esquina noroeste.\
\
Thoroniel espera saber que has derrotado a las arañas que merodean por los Valles Trenzados.","Combatiendo a la Camada","'Has llegado justo a tiempo, ${PLAYER}; de haber tardado más, las arañas de los Valles Trenzados podrían haberse desbordado desde su valle y haberme obligado a retirarme. Una vez que esas criaturas escapen del valle, habrá poco que las detenga antes de alcanzar el resto del Bosque de los Trolls. Imladris se convertiría en el único faro en la oscuridad, aunque puede que ya lo sea.\
\
'Estas arañas son de una especie particularmente peligrosa, o ya habría entrado al valle para enfrentarlas yo mismo, pero no puedo hacerlo solo. Si puedes, reúne a todos los aliados que puedas, ${PLAYER}, y limpia los Valles Trenzados de esta inmundicia.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad completa.</rgb>","Thoroniel ha estado vigilando la actividad de las arañas en el Bosque de los Trolls Norte y se ha alarmado por el reciente aumento en su número.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad completa.</rgb>","Derrota arañas en los Valles Trenzados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Arañas derrotadas en los Valles Trenzados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las arañas han hecho su hogar en los Valles Trenzados del Bosque de los Trolls Norte, al norte del campamento de Thoroniel.\
\
Thoroniel te ha pedido que derrotes a las arañas en los Valles Trenzados, y te recomienda llevar aliados.","Habla con Thoroniel"},
[5275]={"'Al llegar desde la Bodega Putrefacta, vimos mucho del hongo en las Obras Hidráulicas. Necesitamos tomar medidas rápidas para asegurarnos de que no nos abrumen, y también, debemos asegurarnos de que los Orcos no mantengan ni siquiera un pequeño punto de apoyo cerca de nuestras ruedas de agua.\
\
'Habla con los demás y haz lo que puedas para ayudarlos con sus planes. Mientras tanto, tengo otra petición para ti.'","Ansurr se encuentra en Hulwul-nefekh, en el centro de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Regresa con él para informarle que has ayudado a sus compañeros con sus ideas.","Ayuda a Gyrgir","Los enanos de Hulwul-nefekh tienen muchas ideas y teorías sobre cómo eliminar el hongo.","Habla con Ansurr en Hulwul-nefekh","'Te agradezco por ayudar a mis compañeros con sus planes. Estoy seguro de que algunos hicieron más que otros, pero todos han demostrado ser valiosos.\
\
'Creo que estamos cerca de descubrir cómo detener este maldito hongo.'","Ayuda a Ansurr","Luchando contra el hongo","'Habla con los demás. Tienen buenas ideas... pero lo más importante, están interesados en quedarse y luchar contra esta maldita aflicción.'","Ansurr y los otros enanos se encuentran en Hulwul-nefekh, en el centro de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Ansurr te ha pedido que ayudes a los otros enanos con sus ideas para combatir el crecimiento malvado.","Ayuda a Thrand"},
[5276]={"'¡Un buen trofeo! Este orco era demasiado peligroso para permitirle seguir con vida, y me alegra saber que ha desaparecido de una vez por todas.'\
\
Eilíefr observa largamente el anillo que le has traído, con el ceño fruncido por la preocupación.\
\
'El anillo del general Talug está extrañamente caliente, ${PLAYER}, a pesar del aire gélido. Recuerda a su dueño. Me pregunto si Talug está realmente muerto…'","El general Talug puede encontrarse en Fil Gashan, muy al suroeste de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
El enano Eilíefr te ha pedido que derrotes al general Talug para demostrar tu valía y que regreses con su anillo cuando lo hayas conseguido.","Anillo del general Talug obtenido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Devuelve el anillo a Eilíefr en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","'¡Así que tú eres ${CLASS:el poderoso[m]|la poderosa[f]}  del que todo el mundo habla tan bien! Los rumores de tu valor y coraje han llegado a mis oídos, pero como soy de naturaleza escéptica, me gustaría comprobar por mí mismo si estás a la altura del desafío que tengo que proponerte.\
\
'Muchos de nosotros esperamos frustrar las malvadas intenciones de los orcos de atacar el Bosque de Oro de los elfos. Si de verdad eres todo lo que dicen, irás al corazón de Fil Gashan y te enfrentarás al líder que comanda sus fuerzas: el general Talug. Quiero que derrotes a este orco y me traigas su anillo como prueba de que ha muerto.\
\
'No será una tarea sencilla, pero tampoco es imposible. Demuestra tu valía en este desafío que te ofrezco y recibirás una generosa recompensa. Ah, y… no hay ninguna deshonra en llevar amigos contigo en esta empresa.'","Fil Gashan sirve como cuartel y campo de entrenamiento de los orcos de Moria. Tras esos muros, un temible general ha estado preparando a sus tropas para un asalto contra los elfos de Lothlórien, al este de Khazad-dûm. Los enanos de Brogur y Bósi, que desean recuperar Moria, pretenden impedirlo a cualquier precio, pues anhelan que elfos y enanos restauren sus antiguas alianzas en beneficio de ambos pueblos.","Fil Gashan: el anillo del general","'Me gustaría mucho ver una prueba de la derrota de Talug. Tráeme su anillo… si puedes.'","Recoge el anillo del general Talug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5277]={"Regresa con Geirr en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Enemigos muertos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Tu fama se ha extendido por estos largos túneles, . Sí, deja de lado la modestia; puedo ver en tu ojos la mirada brillante de ${PLAYERNAME:un aventurero[m]|una aventurera[f]} valiente. Reconocería a los de tu clase incluso sin que los rumores me lo confirmaran.\
\
'¿Te apuntas a un pequeño reto? Al suroeste de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, las fuerzas de Fil Gashan están planeando un ataque contra nuestros vecinos elfos de Lothlórien, y no debemos permitir que eso suceda. Estamos haciendo todo lo posible por detenerlos, pero apuesto a que te gustaría ayudar, aunque seas ${PLAYERNAME:un forastero[m]|una forastera[f]}.\
\
'${PLAYERNAME:Un aventurero[m]|Una aventurera[f]} como tú no dudaría en aceptar un simple desafío como el que te voy a proponer: ve a Fil Gashan y mata a tantos orcos como puedas. Son muchos; su número no deja de crecer y su amenaza no deja de aumentar.'","'Seré honesto contigo: no estaba seguro de que estuvieras a la altura de este desafío. ¡Pero me alegro de haberme equivocado esta vez! Perdóname por no haber confiado más en ti, ${PLAYER}, pues los rumores sobre tu valentía eran más que ciertos.\
\
'Aquí tienes una muestra de mi agradecimiento. Espero verte más a menudo en los próximos días, puesto que eres de gran ayuda para nuestra causa.'","Fil Gashan sirve como cuartel y campo de entrenamiento de los orcos de Moria. Tras esos muros, un temible general ha estado preparando a sus tropas para un asalto contra los elfos de Lothlórien, al este de Khazad-dûm. Los enanos de Brogur y Bósi, que desean recuperar Moria, pretenden impedirlo a cualquier precio, pues anhelan que elfos y enanos restauren sus antiguas alianzas en beneficio de ambos pueblos.","'¿Por qué aún estás aquí? Hay enemigos que combatir en Fil Gashan.'","Fil Gashan - Debilitar a las fuerzas enemigas","Mata enemigos en Fil Gashan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El enano Geirr se encuentra al suroeste de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
El enano Geirr te ha retado a adentrarte en Fil Gashan y derrotar a muchos de los orcos que allí habitan.","El enano Geirr se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, al noreste de Fil Gashan.\
\
Geirr querrá saber si has sido lo bastante valiente como para adentrarte en Fil Gashan y pelear contra los orcos."},
[5278]={"Sigurd espera noticias de tu incursión en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, al noreste de Fil Gashan.\
\
El general Talug ha sucumbido ante ti y has logrado pasar entre los centinelas uruk casi sin que te descubriesen. Sigurd querrá saber si has cumplido todas las condiciones de su difícil desafío.","Fil Gashan - Asalto Sigiloso","'¿El general Talug sigue vivo? ¡Es imperdonable! ¡Vuelve ahora mismo y derrótalo!'","Fil Gashan está muy al suroeste de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, y el general Talug se encuentra en las profundidades de aquel sitio.\
\
Sigurd te ha retado a que utilices el sigilo y el ingenio para vencer al general Talug, el líder de una gran horda de orcos, sin matar a demasiados de sus centinelas.","'¡Estoy tremendamente impresionado! Has hecho honor a tu fama, un gran honor, sin duda. Pero hay algo que aún me preocupa. Según tu descripción de este enemigo, parece que el mal no se mantendrá a raya por mucho tiempo en Fil Gashan.\
\
'¿Crees que Talug se ha ido para siempre? Sé que lo viste sucumbir, pero mi corazón me dice que volverá en poco tiempo. Una criatura tan dura y malvada no suele caer tras una sola derrota. Recuerda lo que te digo: pronto habrá problemas de nuevo...'","'Se rumorea que eres más fuerte que la mayoría, . Admito que pareces lo bastante valiente, y tienes una mirada más feroz que la de muchos que he visto. Quizás podrías hacer frente a un enemigo muy difícil que amenaza nuestra causa.\
\
'He oído que hay un enemigo mortal que lidera a la chusma en Fil Gashan, un orco llamado general Talug. Te ofrezco el mayor de todos los desafíos que pueda darte: enfrentarte a este rival.\
\
'Y, sin embargo, el mero hecho de pelear contra el general Talug no será más que una nimiedad para ${PLAYERNAME:un poderoso[m]|una poderosa[f]}  como tú. Si buscas un verdadero desafío, ten cuidado de no matar a demasiados de los centinelas de Talug. En Fil Gashan hay herramientas que te ayudarán con esta tarea, y si logras llevarla a cabo, quedaré muy impresionado. Asegúrate de llevar compañeros audaces a esta aventura.'","Centinelas muertos (${NUMBER})","No mates a más de 2 centinelas (${NUMBER} muertos)","General Talug derrotado","Fil Gashan sirve como cuartel y campo de entrenamiento de los orcos de Moria. Tras esos muros, un temible general ha estado preparando a sus tropas para un asalto contra los elfos de Lothlórien, al este de Khazad-dûm. Los enanos de Brogur y Bósi, que desean recuperar Moria, pretenden impedirlo a cualquier precio, pues anhelan que elfos y enanos restauren sus antiguas alianzas en beneficio de ambos pueblos.","Regresa con Sigurd en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Derrota al general Talug"},
[5279]={"Deliver the mugs to Barliman Butterbur at the entrance to the inn.","Coaxed drunken revellers off tables in the Prancing Pony (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'They left the mugs where?! Goodness me, I don't think I'd ever have found them. Not in a crowd like this!\
\
'I do hope none of the patrons were upset by my request. The folk come to celebrate Midsummer seem a good-natured sort, but I would not be much of an inn-keeper if there were no inn left to keep!\
\
'You have been a great help, ${PLAYER}. Can I offer you something?'","Barliman Butterbur, proprietor of the Prancing Pony, has found himself pleasantly overwhelmed during Bree's celebration of Midsummer.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","Drunken revellers and forsaken mugs can be found throughout the Prancing Pony in Bree.\
\
Barliman has asked you to coax drunken revellers off the tables before they can kick more of his crockery into the corners of the Prancing Pony. He has also asked you to gather any mugs abandoned by drunken revellers in unusual spots in the inn.","Find and retrieve abandoned mugs in the Prancing Pony (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hello and welcome to the Prancing Pony!\
\
'Have you come to join in Bree-town's celebration of Midsummer? You would certainly not be the first, I must tell you. It has so often been my duty to alert adventurers like yourself to the needs of others, but I must confess that today, it is I who must ask something of you. You see... even with Bob and Nob about to help me, I was woefully unprepared for how many customers Midsummer would bring to Bree-town!\
\
'Before you join in the festivities and find yourself as merry as some of my patrons, could you do me a favour? Some of the patrons have taken a bit too much to drink and have found themselves atop my tables. Normally, such practices do not bother me, but they've begun to damage my crockery and I've no time to step out to speak to them myself. Also, Nob informed me that they've taken to leaving their mugs in the strangest of places about the Pony.\
\
'Find as many mugs as you can and coax the most drunken of the revellers down off my tables, would you? But do not be too harsh with them!'","Filled to the Brim","Deliver the mugs to Barliman Butterbur","Found and retrieved abandoned mugs in the Prancing Pony (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Coax drunken revellers off tables in the Prancing Pony (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[5280]={"Baranor can be found at the keep in Arnach.\
\
You have helped Dagor and Indir work against the invading Haradrim, as Baranor asked. Now you should return to Baranor in Arnach.","Filling Forlong's Shoes","Baranor's two captains are busy guarding the town and keeping watch on the Haradrim who have snuck into Lossarnach.","Dagor and Indir can be found at the keep in Arnach.\
\
Baranor has asked you to help his two captains, Dagor and Indir, protect the town from the Haradrim.","Talk to Baranor","Help Dagor and Indir","'${PLAYER}! There's no time now. The Haradrim - they're planning an attack. Ah, what shall we do? We mustn't stand around. We must act!'","'The truth is, Lord Forlong left me with too many men. We sent as many as we could up to Imloth Melui, but the lads with war in their eyes couldn't bear to be cooped up behind those walls. I couldn't handle them all myself, so I made Dagor and Indir my captains.\
\
'Like the sun and moon, those two are! Dagor's the more soldierly and fit for the role. Whereas Indir is clever and steady enough, but he worries and broods. We have enough darkness from the skies above! A captain should keep his head high.'","'Ah, would that I were off, marching with Forlong to war! Still, I will not let ill chance rob me of any glory. There are enemies in Lossarnach, now, and I may prove my mettle as a captain and warrior here, as well.\
\
'Baranor sees. He smiles on me, and when Forlong returns victorious, Baranor will tell him of my deeds.'","'Ah, yes! Where was I? Welcome to Arnach! I can't give you half the welcome old Lord Forlong would do. But he's gone off to Minas Tirith - off to war - and here I am! Baranor, Captain of the Guard, is who I am, and I must do my best to fill his shoes. Only he left me with such a great lot of green lads, all restless and rousting about. It's like herding mice!\
\
'So I've made captains of Dagor and Indir. There's Dagor over there. Destined for greatness, if you ask me. At any rate, between guarding Arnach and keeping watch on these damned Haradrim, we three have had our hands full, and then some!\
\
'Now you look a well-travelled and sensible ${RACE}. Could you lend my captains a hand? I assure you, Arnachrim lives depend on it!'","'Do not let my furrowed brows weigh on your heart, ${CLASS}. \
\
'Dagor plays at war and good-hearted Baranor keeps watch over the township as if these were times of peace. While I would curb the one and rouse the other, to do so would be out of my place. So I, who harbour no dreams of war and glory, take the burden willingly. I will plan and brood so that their dreams are not darkened... and so Arnach remains safe.'"},
[5281]={"'Ah, so you want to give it a try? It's not easy, I'll tell you that! You've seen the ice sculptures in Winter-home, have you not? My work is brilliant, at least most of the time...\
\
'I'll admit, I've been having more trouble with this project than my last. I simply can't keep this field filled and the mayor is getting frustrated. Whether it's the winter conditions or some of those blasted snow-beasts, my snowmen keep getting destroyed.\
\
'It's hard to stay passionate when your work is wrecked every single day. Maybe you can help though. See if you can craft more of my snowmen and make this field an amazing sight to behold!'","'I like the way you work. Your work is almost as good as mine...maybe you can help me out some more tomorrow. I'm sure if you keep trying, you can do even better!\
\
'Here are some coins for your hard work.'","Build one of Virgil's snowmen","In the field outside of Winter-home, select the style of snowman you'd like to build.","'Well, which one do you want to build?'","Talk to Virgil Greenfield","Filling The Field","Virgil Greenfield needs help filling out the snowman field outside of Winter-home. He has directed you to try your hand at crafting one of his snowmen.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>"},
[5282]={"'This poison upon the blade of this dagger is secreted by the slugs that dwell in the marshes to the east. It is quite deadly and must be collected with much care. Perhaps that is where the leader of these brigands skulks?\
\
'If so, he should be dealt with...perhaps if you are able to dispatch him, his followers will return to the Stonedeans and leave us in peace.'","Dudsig is near the stables in Oserley, west of the marshes.\
\
You should return to Dudsig with news of your success.","Filth and Corruption","Defeat Eldnoth","DNT -- Will not be seen","Defeated Eldnoth","'You survived the marshes? With all the poisonous slugs, I was not sure one unaccustomed to these lands would have come out alive.\
\
'I must congratulate you!'","The brigand leader may be found in the marshes east of Oserley.\
\
Dudsig has asked you to find and defeat the leader of the brigands who assaulted Lúfa.","You reported the success of your duty at Ordlac's house and delivered the dagger you found to Dudsig.","Talk to Dudsig in Oserley"},
[5286]={"You have successfully brought these pure waters to the source of the Morgulduin in hopes of beginning the process of purifying the tainted river. You have done a great service to all those working to reclaim Minas Ithil from the remnants of Sauron's forces.","Add pure water to the source of the Morgulduin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Arodor has asked me to give you these phials. They were brought to us by the Elves of Lothlórien and contain pure waters from high mountain springs. We believe that if this water is brought to the source of the Morgulduin River, it may begin to cleanse itself of the years of defilement. If you are to venture inside the Filth-well of Eithel Gwaur, bring these phials with you and begin the process to purify the river.'","The waters of the Morgulduin are deadly at its source.\
\
You should attempt to purify the deadly waters of the Morgulduin River.","Added pure water to the source of the Morgulduin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Filth-well: Restoring the Morgulduin","There is much for the White Company to accomplish in reclaiming Minas Ithil from the remnants of Sauron's forces.","Completado"},
[5287]={"Defeated Ilmabiri rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sewer rats can be found throughout Ilmabiri, but may be more plentiful in Gedma-ghâr, on the eastern edge.","You have slain many Ilmabiri rats. Return to Gajóta to let him know.","Defeat Ilmabiri rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Making yourself useful, are you? Why don't you do something more practical like helping me? Helping me helps all of us, as I'm the one keeping everyone fed!' \
\
Gajóta exclaims this loudly for all to hear. The other smugglers groan as if this is something they have heard many times before.\
\
'Unfortunately, I am not only keeping my clansmen fed but the neighbours as well. Sewer rats keep getting into our food stores! I tell them we need to get a cat like on a ship, but do we have a cat? We do not.\
\
'If you want to be of use to us, go find those filthy thieves and rid us of them.'","Gajóta, the cook at Hêbatokh, the Morutágya clan hideout, has asked you to do something about the rats that keep getting into their food stores.","'Ah, the hero returns! Did you deal with those wretched things?'\
\
You tell him you did.\
\
'Very good! Now you have accomplished something of import. Here, you deserve some food for your trouble.'","Filthy Thieves","Talk to Gajóta"},
[5288]={"'Among the tasks that I have set you to, I want you to speak with Ulferth, the captain of these brigand treasure-seekers. Tell him that we will allow his band to leave peacefully, but they must leave behind all the relics that they stole from the Field of Celebrant.\
\
'Ulferth is oft seen at the edge of their encampment at Atburg. This offer will only be open for a short time. If he refuses, then we shall take more drastic measures.\
\
'Return to Eowils, our scout outside Atburg, with Ulferth's answer.'","Aculf wants to make it clear that the brigands are not welcome in the territory of the Riddermark, although he is willing to entertain a peaceful resolution.","Talk to Ulferth at Atburg in the Rushgore","'This is it, then. Ulferth has refused my demands. He shall rue the day he ever came to the Rushgore....'","Eowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp.\
\
Aculf instructed you to bring Ulferth's answer to the scout Eowils.","Talk to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore","Final Notice","Ulferth can be found at the edge of Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore.\
\
Aculf asked you to deliver his ultimatum to Ulferth, captain of the treasure-seekers in the Rushgore.","'Are you serious? The horse-boy wants us to leave? The Field of Celebrant is rife with relics and trinkets from which my men and I can make a fortune...tell your friend that if he wants us gone, he will have to move us himself.'"},
[5289]={"Wights can be found among the cairns east along the road above the Bone Quarry.\
\
Naeglanc has asked you to banish any wights you might find around the cairns in the eastern valley.","Defeated wights in the eastern valley (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat wights in the eastern valley (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mair can be found in the eastern valley above the Bone Quarry.\
\
Naeglanc asked you to speak with Mair.","'Along the valley wall above the Bone Quarry, a small set of cairns trail further to the west. A large number of wights have been drawn to this area for some unknown reason.\
\
'Can you seek out the wights in these cairns and banish them from the Bonevales? It is troubling that the foul demons have begun to move more freely.\
\
'Travel eastwards along the ridge above the Bone Quarry and follow the valley to its end. There you will find the cairns in question. When you have done this, seek Mair among the cairns.'","Naeglanc and his allies continue to battle the evil wights and spirits which have arisen within the Bonevales.","Final Rest","'Mair is encamped above the Bone Quarry.'","'Deal with those wights, then speak with Mair.'","'Thank you for sending these abominations to oblivion. The evil they represent cannot be tolerated in these sacred lands.'","Talk to Mair among the cairns"},
[5290]={"Final Stand","Gárwig, Thrymm and Cyneberg have gathered in the Mead Hall in Forlaw to prepare for the final stand against Núrzum.\
\
Speak with Thrymm and let him know you are ready to end Núrzum's path of destruction once and for all.","'With Núrzum gone, we can begin to deal with the great losses we've suffered and finally rebuild Wildermore and our lives. We couldn't possibly repay you for all that you've done for us, ${PLAYER}.'","Speak with Thrymm","Thrymm has returned to the Forlaw Mead Hall.\
\
You should speak with him after the great victory.","'The time has come, ${PLAYER}. We must finish this and defeat Núrzum once and for all.'","With Thrymm's return, the time to strike Núrzum is now.","Speak with Thrymm in the Forlaw Mead Hall","'Let us end this now!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>"},
[5291]={"'¡Oh, que nunca hubieran venido a estas tierras malditas!'","'¡Mis hijos, mis pobres hijos!'","'Las noticias que has traído me afligen profundamente, porque Amlach era joven y fuerte, y lo amaba mucho. La única consolación en mi pena es que murió buscando a su hermano, a quien amaba más que al miedo que sentía por ese lugar espantoso.\
\
'Si este diario dice la verdad, entonces Amlach aún creía que había esperanza para su hermano, aunque mi corazón teme lo peor.\
\
'Por favor, ${PLAYER}, busca el túmulo sobre el pantano donde Amlach oyó a su hermano, tráeme a mi hijo sano y salvo.'","Tu búsqueda de los hijos desaparecidos de Addie encontró los restos de Amlach Trigal, que sostenía el diario de su hermano. Las últimas entradas crípticas parecen revelar que Amlach oyó voces siniestras provenientes de las regiones del sur de las Quebradas de los Túmulos","'¡Déjame en paz!'","El diario que encontraste parece indicar que Malin fue llevado al sur de las Quebradas de los Túmulos, a un túmulo que da al pantano maligno.\
\
Addie Trigal te ha pedido que busques a su otro hijo, Malin","Habla con Addie Trigal en el Alto del Hombre Muerto","Malin ha sido derrotado","Busca a Malin","Encuentra a Malin","Al comenzar a examinar a Malin, de pronto el cuerpo se agita...","'¿Qué hay de Malin? ¿Has encontrado alguna señal de Malin? Por favor, encuéntralo'","Addie Trigal espera tu regreso en la relativa seguridad que ofrecen sus guías en el Alto del Hombre Muerto.\
\
En tu búsqueda por las Quebradas de los Túmulos, encontraste a los dos hijos de Addie, Amlach y Malin, pero demasiado tarde para ayudar a cualquiera de los dos. Las criaturas viles de las Quebradas de los Túmulos los habían matado a ambos y tomaron los restos de Malin para sus propios fines. Debes regresar con Addie Trigal y contarle lo que ha sucedido con su hijo.","'Mis dos hijos se han ido. Los tontos, oh los tontos. Querían encontrar riquezas entre los muertos, pero los muertos conservaron lo suyo y reclamaron a mis hijos.\
\
'¡Almas inquietas! ¿Debo unirme a ellos ahora por mi propia necedad? Por favor, por favor, déjame con mi pena'"},
[5292]={"You have bid Agalûnu farewell and she asked you to tell her sister Kalkhadra in Iridír that she is all right.","Shanthar has thanked you for all that you have done. He asked you to visit Agalûnu once more to check on her and tell her he will visit soon.","You have done what you can to help restore balance to Arwáth, for both the forest and the people who will now share the burden of caring for it.","Finding Balance","Talk to Agalûnu","'You have done well ${PLAYER}. There is much more to do, but perhaps with Agalûnu's assistance, I will be able to not only preserve this grove but expand it as well. You have done much to help, particularly in bringing Agalûnu and I together to talk. I now have an ally instead of an enemy.\
\
'I will let you be on your way, but if you do not mind, would you check on Agalûnu? I have a few matters to attend to first, but please tell her I will visit soon and see if I can do anything for her injury. Farewell, ${PLAYER}.'","Return to Kalkhadra in Iridír","'${PLAYER}, you were gone for an age! Though I suppose it only felt that way because I am bored.'\
\
The woman chuckles to herself and she appears to be in higher spirits as well as better health. You tell her that you are leaving, but Shanthar will soon visit.\
\
'Oh! Well, I hope he feels guilty.'\
\
She laughs again, holding up her wounded arm.\
\
'But I will enjoy the company. It is not every day that I can talk to someone thousands of years old! I cannot even imagine such a life. Are you going back to Iridír? Can you please let my sister know that I yet live? Kalkhadra is likely beside herself with worry.'","'There you are! I was about to start marshalling a search party! Where is Agalûnu?!'\
\
You tell Kalkhadra that her sister is injured but all right, and that an Elf of the Kintai is looking out for her. Kalkhadra's jaw drops.\
\
'Surely you jest. Nobody has seen a Kinta in ages! Oh, Agalûnu... this is what she gets for not being properly afraid of things. You have my thanks for finding her.'"},
[5293]={"'I - I wish you brought me better news, or my Baradûm. I know hope is a favourite drink of fools, and yet for a time it was my only companion. It has now abandoned me, and all I have left are my memories of Baradûm.\
\
'Thank you for this news. It is not what I wished to hear, but at least now I know the truth.'","Check the body to determine if it is Baradûm","Search for clues as to Baradûm's whereabouts (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Return to Galêris with the news of Baradûm's death.","Return to Galêris with the news of Baradûm's death","You see a body nearby. You should check if it is Baradûm","Finding Baradûm","Search for Baradûm in Jâr Obadal.","'Yes, my husband is missing. Will you help me find him?\
\
'He ventured with the others near Jâr Obadal. I fear the spiders have taken him. Two search parties have gone missing.\
\
'Would you aid in the search for him? I am close to breaking. I fear for him so.'","Search for clues to Baradûm's whereabouts. Galêris mentioned he was last seen patrolling near the caves of Jâr Obadal. Jâr Obadal can be found south-east of Ingar-garâsh.","Galêris, one of Mizâdi's Subuzûri in Ingar-garâsh, has asked you to rescue her husband Baradûm. Baradûm was last seen patrolling near the cave of Jâr Obadal, home of ravenous spiders.","Search for Baradûm in Jâr Obadal","Found clues as to Baradûm's whereabouts (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Check the body to determine if it is Baradûm."},
[5294]={"Talk to Berkha","The duckling tilts his head at you, as if quietly asking 'Why were you swimming around in that lake?'\
\
When you reach down to pick him up, he happily leaps into your arms.\
\
He's had his fun. It's time to return to Raghda-gûn.","Berkha announced his presence at the shore of Irkhadâr.\
\
Speak to Berkha.","As you approach, Berkha cradled safely in your arms, you see that Raghda-gûn has more guests. One of them, a familiar greasy looking man, lies dazed on the ground, his vacant eyes fixed on the sky above. The other two you may have seen in passing on the streets of Halrax.\
\
'Berkha!' Raghda-gûn shouts as you approach. 'What have I told you about going off on your own?'\
\
Berkha quacks and nips at your sleeve.\
\
'We will speak later, young man.'\
\
Raghda-gûn fixes her clever eyes on you.\
\
'You have my thanks. Now, I believe you know this gentleman taking up space on the ground?'","Finding Berkha","Talk to Raghda-gûn","Find Berkha","'I hate to ask this of you, but could you track down Berkha? I would normally have a friend go search, but the turmoil in recent months has seen many rocs find new perches in calmer seas.\
\
'Hmm? Do I not have a mate to help protect my nest? Alas, he is no longer with me.\
\
'What? No he's not dead. His mother is ill so he went to go care for her. What did you think I meant?\
\
'Anyway, please go find Berkha. Perhaps he went down near the caldera lake where I first found him.'","Raghda-gûn asked you to find Berkha in Irkhadâr, the caldera lake in Zamarzîr.\
\
Irkhadâr is north of Aklâradum.","You find a few duck feathers. Perhaps Berkha has been nearby","You have found little Berkha and should take him back to Aklâradum.\
\
Aklâradum is on a cliff to the south of Irkhadâr.","Sadly, there is no sign of Berkha","Search for signs of Berkha at Irkhadâr (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You hear a loud quacking from the lakeside shore.","There is no sign of Berkha here","The little bird, Berkha, has gone missing! His mother, Raghda-gûn, has bid you find him."},
[5295]={"'Oh, wonderful! Look how happy Draug is!\
\
'I must admit, I'd begun to worry that 'Blue' was lost for good. I could have sewn another, of course, but it would never have been quite the same. And besides, Draug would have figured it out!\
\
'I cannot thank you enough, ${PLAYER}.'","Dírion's dog, Draug, is disheartened after losing his favourite toy, a doll called 'Blue', somewhere in the woods around Alagrant.","Search the traps in the woods around Alagrant for 'Blue'","Finding Blue","Draug can be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found 'Blue' in one of the traps outside Alagrant. You should return 'Blue' to Draug in Alagrant.","Draug howls in excitement and practically snatches 'Blue' from your hand!","The sprung trap can be found outside Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found a small blue object caught in one the traps. You should free 'Blue' from the trap.","Deliver 'Blue' to Draug in Alagrant","'Blue' appears to be a doll made in the likeness of the Men of the Mountain","Free 'Blue' from the sprung trap","Talk to Dírion","Dírion can be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have returned 'Blue' to Draug and he appears pleased. You should talk to Dírion.","A small, colourful object caught in a nearby trap catches your eye. It's 'Blue'!","'${PLAYER}? I had not heard that you'd returned to the Vale. What business brings you here?'\
\
You inform Dírion that you are one of King Elessar's emissaries in Gondor, and that you have come to aid the people of the Blackroot Vale.\
\
'Oh, I—you must excuse the manner of my behaviour when last you visited the Vale. I was perhaps too vocal in my displeasure with the Steward's leadership, and you did not deserve such a harsh welcome to Alagrant. But, if you are here to aid us...'\
\
Dírion appears embarrassed, and his face flushes red.\
\
'You see, Draug has lost his favourite toy somewhere in the woods, and try as I may, I haven't been able to find it. Draug could likely find it himself, but there are traps about, and I would not risk him stepping into one of them. I call his toy 'Blue' because... it is blue, and well, you'll understand.\
\
'Would you please take a look in the traps outside Alagrant? If it's not in one of those, it's probably lost, but I would appreciate your help just the same, my friend.'","Traps can be found outside the hamlet of Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Dírion has asked you to search the traps outside Alagrant for any sign of 'Blue', a beloved toy of his dog, Draug. You should search the traps in the woods around Alagrant.","This trap is empty, and you see no sign of 'Blue'..."},
[5296]={"Recoge bayas ácidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Cuántas bayas! Esto es excelente. Eres increíble, de verdad, ${PLAYER}.'","En busca de un postre fresco","Recoge bayas ácidas que crecen al oeste de donde Barhador ha acampado en el Ángulo del Mitheithel.","Bayas ácidas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vuelve con Barhador a su campamento en el Ángulo del Mitheithel con las bayas que has recogido.","'¿Te gusta mi escudo? El tío Candaith dice que es de las Tierras Brunas. ¿Has estado alguna vez allí? ¿De dónde eres? ¿Has dicho que conoces a Halbarad? ¿Conoces al tío Candaith? Es muy valiente y fuerte.'\
\
El muchacho te asalta a preguntas y no te permite contestar a ninguna.\
\
'¡Voy a ser un Montaraz como él! Mataré orcos y trasgos, y tendré mi propio arco y espada. Viajaré por todo Eriador y haré cosas buenas por la gente, pero nunca lo sabrán. Así somos. Por cierto, ¿quién eres?\
\
'Me llamo Barhador. ¿Vas a buscar más comida y a unirte a nosotros? ¡No tenemos nada de postre! ¿Te gustan las bayas? Al oeste de aquí crecen unas bayas que son dulces y ácidas a la vez, y te hacen poner esta cara.'\
\
El chico frunce los labios y levanta las cejas todo lo que puede.\
\
'Pasamos por allí antes, pero Ivoreth dijo que aún no podíamos detenernos. Si vas a recolectar, ¿puedes traernos algunas? ¡Están muy buenas, te lo prometo!'","Entre otras muchas cosas, Barhador te ha pedido que recojas algunas bayas ácidas mientras estás fuera buscando otras cosas para comer.","Vuelve con Barhador con las bayas ácidas"},
[5297]={"Apply the poultice","Hierbas curativas recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Would you please collect some healing herbs? There should be some growing across the stream to the south-east. I have a mortar and pestle you can use to mash them.'","Finding Healing","You have collected herbs to make a healing poultice for Agalûnu. You should mash them with the mortar and pestle near Agalûnu's tent.","'Thank you so much ${PLAYER}. Hopefully, that will do to avert festering. I should continue to rest and allow my body to heal. I feel ashamed though. I told Shanthar that I would return and help him steward the forest. He will think I lied to him when I fail to return.\
\
'On my honour ${PLAYER}, I was speaking true. I beg you to go to him and tell him of my condition and reassure him that I intend to keep my oath.'","Collect healing herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Agalûnu","You have made a healing poultice. You should go to Agalûnu and apply it to her wound.","Mix the herbs with a mortar and pestle","'${PLAYER}, I fear that travelling to visit Shanthar has caused my wound to re-open. It is terribly painful, and now I worry that it may fester. I know how to make a poultice, but I cannot gather the ingredients. I do not feel well at all.\
\
'${PLAYER}, would you please collect some healing herbs? There should be some growing across the stream to the south-east. I have a mortar and pestle you can use to mash them.'","Talk to Shanthar","Agalûnu has asked you to collect healing herbs for a poultice. They can be found across the stream to the south-east.","Agalûnu must rest to allow her wound to heal. In the meantime, she asked you to return to Shanthar and reassure him that she intends to keep her promise to help him care for the forest. Shanthar is at his abode in Arwáth.","'You return without Agalûnu?'\
\
The Kinta looks irritated. You tell him of her injury and that she is resting. You also reassure him that she is determined to keep her promise to him once she has recovered. The Elf's brow furrows.\
\
'I confess ${PLAYER} that I have not spent much time in the company of Men and I forgot that they do not heal with the ease of the Firstborn. I am no master of the healing arts, but I believe rest and your poultice should serve her well.\
\
'It gladdens my heart to know she intends to keep her oath. I look forward to teaching others how to care for the grove. Never did I think anyone other than Kintai would be interested in doing such a thing.'","Agalûnu's wound has re-opened and she worries about a possible infection.","You have made a healing poultice and applied it to Agalûnu's wound. You should talk to her and see how she is doing.","'I beg you to go to Shanathar and tell him of my condition. Reassure him that I intend to keep my oath.'"},
[5298]={"Meneldor has failed to return to the agreed-upon meeting location. Landroval grows concerned for his friend's safety, as the spider-hole to the west remains the most likely unsearched location.","Talk to Landroval","Finding Meneldor","You have found the cave-entrance","Locate the entrance of the spider-cave","Venom-bite spider-cave lies west of Landroval's hidden clearing.\
\
Landroval has asked you to search inside the spider-lair for his missing friend, Meneldor.","'Be on guard, for there are foul things which may lurk in the dark. Gather your courage and seek out the cave in the hills to the west.'","'I believe that Meneldor may be in great danger. He should have returned by now. It is not in his nature to ignore a meeting, yet there is no trace of him in these hills.\
\
'Only one location remains unsearched. I do not wish to place you in such danger, but I dare not go there myself. There is a cavern to the west of here that appears inhabited by spiders. Such a place is treacherous for an Eagle! Explore the cave and attempt to locate Meneldor within.'","Venom-bite spider-cave lies west of Landroval's hidden clearing.\
\
Landroval has requested that you discover the entrance to the spider-lair he viewed to the west.","Landroval can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of the Wailing Hills.\
\
Landroval awaits your return and will be eager to see his friend Meneldor as well.","Enter the cave and search for Meneldor","'I am relieved to see you again... and still whole and hale. You have done us a great service, and we shall not soon forget the aid that you have lent us, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[5299]={"'No puedo creerlo. Bali... se ha ido. ¡Debe ser vengado! Y este diario dice lo que hay detrás de esto: una reina araña de las Montañas Azules. Ella y su prole deben haberme seguido desde las Salas de Thorin.\
\
'¡Sepan esto! Incluso si soy asesinado, ella nunca dejará este lugar... ha encontrado presas fáciles aquí. ¡Debemos destruirla, o Archet se convertirá en un nuevo hogar para la reina y su descendencia!'","La entrada a la cueva que los cazadores bloquearon está en las ruinas al este de Archet.\
\
Atli te dijo que envió a su primo Bali a revisar las cuevas, pero aún no ha regresado. Si lo encuentras, puede que tenga la respuesta a lo que ha perturbado a las arañas.","Páginas faltantes del diario encontradas (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'No creo que pueda ayudarte. El primo de Atli debe estar por ahí en alguna parte de la cueva.'","Llevar el diario y las páginas del diario a Atli Matarañas","Buscar a Bali","Habla con Atli Matarañas en Archet","Las páginas faltantes del diario de Bali deben estar en algún lugar dentro de las cuevas. Es posible que las arañas hayan tomado las páginas y las hayan envuelto en sus capullos.\
\
Has encontrado el cadáver de Bali y su diario, pero faltan varias páginas. Debes encontrar las páginas antes de regresar con Atli.","'¡Bien, has regresado! Parece que aquí hay mucho más de lo que pensé al principio. Mientras estabas fuera, llegó mi primo Bali, y lo envié a buscar algunas cuevas en las ruinas fuera de la muralla este de Archet. Algunos cazadores habían dejado caer una enorme piedra frente a la cueva, y quería que él se asegurara de que la piedra permaneciera. Aún no ha regresado, y estoy preocupado.\
\
'Ahora bien, por lo que me dijiste de los problemas de Sprigley, las arañas salieron por el sótano de su cobertizo. Quizá al ver la cueva bloqueada, cavaron un túnel por allí.\
\
'No lo sabremos con certeza hasta que encuentres a Bali. Con suerte, él tendrá algunas respuestas.'","'¡Ve a buscar a Bali rápido antes de que ocurra algo terrible! Lo envié a las cuevas en las ruinas al este de aquí.'","Registras el cadáver de Bali y encuentras un diario con varias páginas faltantes. El texto del diario dice:\
\
'No lo creería, pero las arañas han despejado la entrada de la cueva. He entrado en la cueva y las arañas reaccionaron instantáneamente, como si fueran atraídas por mí. No sé por qué. Pasé el día buscando cuidadosamente solo cerca de la entrada y encontré varios cadáveres envueltos en capullos. ¡Estas arañas parecen envolver todo en sus capullos! Escribiré más mañana cuando me adentre más en la cueva.'\
\
Quizá lo mejor sea entrar en la cueva para ver si puedes encontrar el resto de las páginas del diario antes de regresar con Atli.","'Esas arañas subieron por mi cobertizo en el extremo más alejado de la granja, pero deberías hablar con Atli antes de ir allí de nuevo. Estoy seguro de que él sabrá más sobre qué hacer.'","Encontrar páginas faltantes del diario (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Atli Matarañas se encuentra justo al norte de Cal Sprigley.\
\
Cal Sprigley sugirió que hables con Atli Matarañas sobre las arañas en su granja y cómo deshacerse de ellas.","Encontrando la razón","Atli Matarañas se puede encontrar en el extremo norte de Archet.\
\
Atli Matarañas querrá saber qué descubriste entre las páginas del diario de Bali.","'¿Has encontrado las páginas faltantes del diario de Bali?'","'Esas arañas se han comido a mis trabajadores y nos han echado a Holly y a mí de nuestro hogar. ¡Debe haber alguna forma de sacarlas de nuestra tierra!\
\
Creo que Atli Matarañas sabe más sobre arañas que yo. Quizá deberías hablar con él otra vez.\
\
¡No podemos volver a casa hasta que esas horribles criaturas se hayan ido!'","La granja de Cal Sprigley ha sido invadida por arañas sin razón aparente, dejando a Cal y Holly sin hogar en Archet.","'¿Bali... muerto? ¡Esto es... imposible! ¿Y las arañas han abierto la cueva? Debes entrar en la cueva y buscar el resto de su diario.\
\
'¡Debemos vengar a Bali, y ese diario puede contener el conocimiento que nos ayude a hacerlo!'"},
[5300]={"Wights have begun to rise up from the cairns of the Bonevales, presenting a threat to all who dwell in Dunland.","Seal cairn-openings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'With the cairns sealed, fewer of the wights can emerge to stalk the land.  It is a shame that this has come to pass.'","'There have been reports of wights rising from the ancient cairns that line the Bone Quarry. These cairns have stood for generations, unsullied until now. We must find a way to close the cairns.\
\
'Will you seek out the cairn-openings and seal the entrances? If so, travel down the path, then east to the Bone Quarry.\
\
'When you have sealed the cairns, find Ilar and tell him of your deed.'","'Have you sealed the cairn-entrances?'","Ilar is at his camp, north and east of the Bone Quarry.\
\
You should seek out Ilar and let him know that the cairns have been sealed.","Talk to Ilar at his camp in the Bonevales","The Bone Quarry lies to the east of Echad Naeglanc.\
\
Naeglanc has asked you to close several cairn-openings within the Bone Quarry.","Sealed cairn-openings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Finding Rest","'Ilar is encamped north of the Bone Quarry.'"},
[5301]={"Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: Treachery","Finding a Breach in the Darkness","Rathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should speak with Rathon and assist him with protecting the Cisterns.","Speak with Rathon","Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Back Door","'Quickly, into the Cisterns!'","'The Withered Tree somehow found a way into the Cisterns and set up encampments there. You would think it a small nuisance but they've been talking with the enemy! There's a raiding party of Orcs in the Cisterns right now and the Withered Tree let them into the city! To think the Withered Tree are Gondorians! We must band together, not fight one another. Please stop them, ${PLAYER}.'","Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Withered Foe","The Withered Tree has taken hold of the Cisterns and let a raiding party of Orcs into the city. It is up to you to regain control of the Cisterns.","Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: Kamabhosh","Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Invaders","'I thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. With time, I hope to drive our enemies back whence they came and restore the Cisterns to their former state.'","Rathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should speak with Rathon."},
[5302]={"Elain awaits you in Lhan Tarren.\
\
You should speak with Elain and inform her that you slew her old enemy.","Defeated Red-eye","'Old Red-eye's cruel howls will trouble the Stag-clan no more! Perhaps now our roosts will remain at peace.\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}. It is almost time for feasting and the telling of tales. You have done quite enough for one day!'","Finding an Old Fiend","Elain, the huntress you rescued not long ago, wishes to finish the hunt she began on the day she was captured.","'The wolf I sought was deep in a den, and I stalked him for many long hours before I became aware that the Dragon-clan was trailing me in the same manner. They took me before I could get too close!'","Talk to Elain at Lhan Tarren","Red-eye was said to be at a den to the south-west.\
\
Elain has asked you to hunt down Red-eye in her stead while she prepares for the evening's rites.","'${PLAYER}! We seem to have a little time left before the Feast of the Stag begins. I wish to finish the hunt I began the day I was taken, but the Elder has asked me to help him prepare for tonight.\
\
'There is an old fiend who has brazenly walked into town and stolen hens from right under our noses. His howl sends a jolt of fear down the spines of my kin. I was stalking him to his den to the south-west while the Draig-lûth rogues were likewise stalking me.\
\
'His name is Red-eye, an evil old menace of a wolf, and I intend to see him on the end of a spear! If you happen to slay him while you are out in the plains, I will be even more impressed with you!'","Defeat Red-eye"},
[5303]={"Several sheep have wandered off and become lost in and near Ahâba.\
\
You should find and <rgb=#00FFFF>whistle</rgb> at the lost sheep to send them home.","Whistled at lost sheep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Finding the Flock","Collect hay bale","Collected hay bale","Shepherd Nahíd in Ahâba needs help finding his lost sheep.","'Welcome to Ahâba, stranger. I am Nahíd, a humble shepherd. If you are here to help, I would appreciate it. My hands are full enough as it is!\
\
'Several of my sheep have wandered off. They should still be nearby, but I fear if I go looking for them, these two in the pen will wander off as well! Would you be willing to find them and bring them back?\
\
'Here, take some of this hay. They cannot resist it! Whistle with it in your hand, and they should come.'","You have found all of Nahíd's lost sheep.\
\
You should return to Nahíd.","Talk to Nahíd","<rgb=#00FFFF>Whistle</rgb> at lost sheep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Nahíd has requested help gathering his sheep.\
\
You should start by collecting the nearby hay bale.","'They have all returned! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Now, we just need to get them into their pen....'"},
[5305]={"Derrota arañas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Buen trabajo! Ahora solo tenemos que encontrar la manera de pasar las telarañas que enredan el nido de arañas.'","'Es bueno que el Oficial sepa lo que ha pasado. Espero que puedas ocuparte de todas esas arañas.'","Encuentra el nido de las arañas","Arañas vencidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'No me hace mucha gracia tener que darte más trabajo, pero parece que las arañas que infestaban mi carreta se han ido a algún sitio. Si crecen y se reproducen, podrían convertirse en una amenaza en otra parte de la Comarca.\
\
'Creo que deberías informar de esto al Oficial de Hobbiton, Robin Madriguera, y ver qué cree que debería hacerse. Normalmente se puede encontrar a Robin Madriguera en la Posada La Mata de Hiedra en el centro de Hobbiton.\
\
'¡Lo último que necesita la Comarca es una infestación de arañas casi tan grandes como un hobbit!'","'Me gustaría poder ayudarte con esas arañas, pero soy un comerciante, no un guerrero.'","Has localizado el origen de las arañas del Bosque del Fardo","La búsqueda del nido","Robin Madriguera se encuentra en la Posada La Mata de Hiedra, en el centro de Hobbiton.\
\
Otho piensa que los Oficiales deberían estar al tanto del peligro que pueden representar las arañas y te ha pedido que hables con Robin Madriguera, el Oficial de Hobbiton.","Robin Madriguera se encuentra en la Posada La Mata de Hiedra, en el centro de Hobbiton.\
\
El Oficial Madriguera te envió a ocuparte de la amenaza que representan las arañas en el Bosque del Fardo y a descubrir la ubicación de su nido. Deberías volver a hablar con Robin Madriguera para contarle que has tenido éxito.","'Otho Anchocinto está en lo cierto al estar preocupado. Ya he recibido informes de que se han visto arañas peligrosas en el Bosque del Fardo, al norte y noroeste de Sobrecolina. Creo que voy a enviarte a investigar este problema.\
\
'Intenta matar tantas arañas como puedas, pero también explora el extremo norte del bosque y ve si puedes encontrar su nido.\
\
'La gente dice que son arañas monstruosamente grandes, así que yo tendría cuidado si fuera tú.'","Puede que haya arañas en el Bosque del Fardo, al norte y noroeste de Sobrecolina.\
\
Otho Anchocinto te envió a hablar con Robin Madriguera sobre las arañas, pero el Oficial de Hobbiton ya había recibido informes sobre las criaturas del Bosque del Fardo. El Oficial Madriguera te ha pedido que mates tantas arañas como puedas, pero también que encuentres su nido.","Otho está preocupado porque las arañas que infestaban su carreta parecen haberse escapado. Podrían representar un peligro en otra parte de la Comarca.","'Tenemos que hacer algo con este problema de arañas. Busca sus nidos en el Bosque del Fardo, al norte y noroeste de Sobrecolina.'","'Por favor, ve a ver al Oficial Robin Madriguera en Hobbiton. Me preocupan todas las arañas que no has encontrado.'"},
[5306]={"After finding the Silent One's home of sorts, the Orc was forced to flee deeper into Lhingris. You and Legolas must now pursue the elusive Orc if you hope to claim his armour.","'Hah! A clever Orc, indeed!\
\
'${PLAYER}, the trails of blood converge here in this swamp!\
\
'Even now, the Silent One must seek shelter in its shallows. We must find him before we lose the path!'","The trails of blood begin at the Silent Haunt and lead deeper into Lhingris.\
\
Legolas has spotted two trails of blood leading from the Silent Haunt. It seems the Silent One is trying to lose you in the shadows of Lhingris.","Follow the trail of the Silent One's blood deeper into Lhingris","The trail of blood leads deeper into Lhingris!","Finding the Path","Talk to Legolas near Dath Nethryn","'${PLAYER}, we must find the Silent One.\
\
'As his face is mostly obscured by his helmet, his armour could be of great use to us in learning more of Shelob and her children. If we can recover his armour, you might gain entry into Cirith Ungol and go unnoticed as one of the many Orcs in its garrison. Indeed, Captain Róglarg even expects the Silent One to report to Cirith Ungol!\
\
'The Silent One knew well enough not to remain here, and he left two trails of blood leading deeper into Lhingris to escape our pursuit. I shall follow one, and you should follow the other.\
\
'Let us see where they lead!'","Legolas can be found above the swamp of Dath Nethryn in Lhingris.\
\
The trails of blood have led both you and Legolas to the swamp of Dath Nethryn. The Silent One now hides within, hoping to tend his wounds and escape your pursuit.","You have found Legolas at the end of the other trail of blood!"},
[5308]={"Return to Penda with the pouches of remedy","This scribbled note contains a set of orders to the Mor-hai Orcs, signed by one named Dushatár. It seems that the Mor-hai have often been careless when creating and handling their poisons. The orders demand that pouches of herbal remedy be carried in order to help cure their mistakes.\
\
It would certainly be helpful to collect some of these remedy pouches and to bring them to Frithstan's camp.","'You have done well to secure this poison remedy. This will help us deal with our injured, and the rest shall be stockpiled to combat further attempts of poisoning by the Mor-hai. Frithstan will be pleased to know of your efforts.'","Penda may be found back at the camp, along the road north of the Cuthstan.\
\
Frithstan and his men should be able to make good use of the remedy you have collected from the Mor-hai.","Collect pouches of the Orcs' poison remedy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Finding the Remedy","A set of orders has been posted, instructing the Mor-hai to carry pouches of remedy in order to safe-guard against their own poisons.","Mor-hai Orcs can be found within their cave in the western section of the Wailing Hills.\
\
Securing remedy from defeated Orcs will likely prove to be a worthwhile endeavour for the Men of Stangard."},
[5310]={"Find and defeat saboteurs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Orc saboteur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Saboteurs are hiding in the cisterns.\
\
You should defeat the saboteurs.","Speak with Rathon","Finding the Saboteurs","Rathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should speak with Rathon.","'Could those who sabotaged the valve actually be from outside the city? Most think there is no way into and out of the city right now with the front gate being heavily guarded, but I know this is false. There are a few cisterns that can take one out of the city. Guards are posted on the lower cisterns at the base of the city but none are posted at the entrances from the mountain. Could Orcs have scaled Mount Mindolluin and snuck in the northern cistern entrance? I shudder at the thought!\
\
'Either way, if the saboteurs are still hiding nearby in the cisterns, they must be apprehended or dealt with in some manner. I leave that to you, my good ${CLASS}.'","'Orcs were trying to sabotage the lesser drainage gates in the cisterns? I assume you dealt with them reasonably then?\
\
'Not only do I not have enough men to maintain the cisterns but now a small band of invaders bide their time under the city. This is a most unfortunate day!'","Rathon has been tasked with maintaining many of the cisterns in Minas Tirith by himself and could use some assistance in tracking down those who sabotaged the main cistern valve."},
[5311]={"Return to Nella","Search for the missing way-stone","You should bring the way-stone back to Nella.\
\
Nella is in Dol Amroth outside of the Swan-knight's Keep.","'Excuse me, I couldn't help but hear that you're going to Hashadir. Oh, pardon me, where are my manners. I'm Nellagwen, but you can call me Nella, and I really need your help. The thing is, I went wandering down to Hashadir a few days ago without knowing it'd been infested with rats. I was horribly surprised when a group of them swarmed me, a terrifying wave of fur and fleas, and I lost my footing. In doing so, I also seem to have dropped the way-stone that I was using to navigate my way around.\
\
'That way-stone belonged to my great, great, great... well, a very long ago ancestor, and it's been passed down in my family for generations. I came here to ask for help getting it back, but as soon as the word \\qrats\\q was mentioned, everyone turned their backs on me.\
\
'Please, I beg you - if you're going to Hashadir, can you look for my way-stone? I need to return it to its safe box before mother finds out that it's missing....'","Finding the Way-finder","You found Nella's way-stone!","'Did you - oh, you found it! Thank you, thank you, thank you! I need to get this back to its safe box right away. Oh, thank you!'","Nella has asked you to you look for her missing way-stone.\
\
The way-stone went missing in Hashadir.","Somewhere in the ruins of Hashadir lies a precious heirloom."},
[5314]={"Recoge trozos de carne de jabalí (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Athelbald will not go back to the farm until his task is complete. You will need to finish it to ensure that he returns safely to the Folde Farm.","Finishing the Task","'I suppose if the danger is that great, I ought to head back to the farm and let you finish my work.\
\
'We do not need much...collecting the meat of a few boars should be plenty for us.'","'You were right...I saw several Orcs on my way back to the farm, and if I had not left when I did, I might not have been able to make it. Thank you for not allowing me to be my stubborn self.'","Talk to Athelbald","Athelbald is at the Folde Farm.\
\
You should bring the boar-meat that you collected to Athelbald.","Trozos de carne de jabalí recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather the meat from four boars.\
\
Boars wander the hills east of the Folde Farm."},
[5315]={"El medallón de Finna","'¡Esto es obra de Finna! Me debes una explicación, ${PLAYER}. ¿Cómo ha llegado a tus manos? Es el único que hay al este de las Montañas Azules, ¡y pertenece a mi buen amigo Nykr!\
\
'...Ah. Supongo que debería decir que perteneció. Qué noticia tan triste.\
\
'Finna es una de las tallistas de nuestra tierra. También es, o más bien era, la amada de Nykr. Su compromiso se formalizó poco antes de que se uniera a esta expedición.\
\
'Muchos remordimientos nos seguirán a casa, y este formará parte de los míos. Cuando hables con Róarr, recuérdale que Nykr tiene un primo, Kuli, a quien también habría que darle la noticia.'","Habla con Róarr en la Guardia Orca","'Le preguntaría a los otros enanos de aquí por qué Nykr valoraba tanto este medallón.'","'Sí, sí, reconozco ese medallón. Pertenece por derecho a un enano llamado Nykr. ¿Cómo es que ha llegado a tus manos?\
\
Roárr se sorprende cuando le cuentas lo que sabes sobre Nykr y la curiosa pieza de joyería.\
\
'¡Pobre Nykr! Así que ha caído. Así que has venido que estas funestas noticias, buscando respuestas a por qué arriesgaría su vida por un objeto tan pequeño. Es una excelente pregunta, pero temo no tener la respuesta. De todos modos, pregunta a los demás enanos aquí en la Guardia Orca sobre ello.'","'Dile a Róarr que el medallón pertenecía a la amada de Nykr, Finna.'","'¿Conoces la historia? ¡Cuéntamela!\
\
'Qué conmovedor... perdóname un momento, creo que, ejem, se me ha metido una esquirla o un poco de polvo en el ojo...\
\
'Mandaré un mensaje a Gufi, y él se encargará de que las noticias lleguen a los seres queridos de Nykr, especialmente a Finna Barbahelada.'","Un enano llamado Nykr se dio la vuelta durante una ruta porque se le había caído un bonito medallón-rompecabezas, y esto le costó la vida. Su amigo Gufi, consternado por esta decisión sin sentido, quiere saber porqué mereció la pena morir por este objeto.","'¿Nykr? Creo que había un Nykr en el Descenso Profundo.\
\
'Oh, ya veo. Lo lamento.\
\
'No, no sé qué significa ese medallón. ¡Te deseo la mejor de las suertes en tu búsqueda!'","'No, no conozco a ningún Nykr. ¿Por qué preguntas?'","'Coincidí con Nykr unas cuantas veces, y una vez me reveló este medallón que guardaba dentro de su camisa. Siempre lo llevaba cerca de su corazón, así que debía significar mucho para él.\
\
'Lo siento, pero no sé más sobre él.'","Hay muchos enanos en la Guardia Orca.\
\
A Róarr le sorprendió la muerte de Nykr. Aunque no sabía por qué su amigo valoraba tanto ese medallón fabricado a mano, te ha sugerido que preguntes a los otros enanos en la Guardia Orca.","'He tomado unas cuantas jarras con Nykr... espero que la piedra le traiga paz, pero nunca había visto este medallón.\
\
'Mis condolencias, para ti y sus parientes.'","Encuentra a un enano en la Guardia Orca que sepa por qué Nykr murió por su medallón","Róarr está en la Guardia Orca.\
\
Róarr querrá saber el significado del medallón, para poder informar de ello a Gufi."},
[5316]={"'Sí, sí, reconozco ese medallón. Pertenece por derecho a un enano llamado Nykr. ¿Cómo es que ha llegado a tus manos?\
\
Roárr se sorprende cuando le cuentas lo que sabes sobre Nykr y la curiosa pieza de joyería.\
\
